COPY public.pages (id, path, hash, title, description, "isPrivate", "isPublished", "privateNS", "publishStartDate", "publishEndDate", content, render, toc, "contentType", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "editorKey", "localeCode", "authorId", "creatorId", extra) FROM stdin;
1	der-program/applications/2025-05-22-elmsworth-cover-email	e4f25dcdb42968f8fb5a	2025-05-22 Elmsworth Cover Email	Cover email from Bill Tran transmitting PXA-2025-0198 and requesting retention of 2023 queue position	f	t				# 2025-05-22 Elmsworth Cover Email\n\n**From:** Bill Tran <bill.tran@cityofelmsworth.gov>\n**To:** DER Program Office <der.program@alleniom.com>\n**Date:** Thu, 22 May 2025 10:47:22 -0500\n**Subject:** PXA-2025-0198 submission — Municipal Service Center PV\n**Cc:** Meera Vellanki <meera.vellanki@alleniom.com>\n\n---\n\nDER Program Office —\n\nAttached please find the City of Elmsworth's DER interconnection application for the Municipal Service Center PV project (Form DIS-APP-01), assigned Application ID PXA-2025-0198 on your intake page. Nameplate is 900 kW AC, behind-the-meter with export capability, mounted on the Municipal Service Center rooftop and adjacent parking canopy.\n\nFor your records, this filing follows our earlier application PXA-2023-0412 dated 04/12/2023 for the same Municipal Service Center site. The 2023 filing sat with our office through a budget cycle change and a facilities director turnover on our side, and we did not push it forward during that period. The scope in the current package is materially the same site, the same 900 kW envelope, and the same point of interconnection area on the mid-town Elmsworth feeder — the update is the CEL-2025-Q2 inverter selection and refreshed drawings dated 05/16/2025.\n\nGiven the continuity of the project, we would like to retain our original 2023 queue position. Council approved the capital allocation in the FY25 budget on the assumption that we would be in construction this fall, and every month we slide back in the queue is a month that pushes mechanical completion past the winter shutdown window and into next spring. We would appreciate your team's confirmation on that point at your earliest convenience so we can lock in permit and procurement dates.\n\nWe are targeting the following applicant-side milestones (also carried in Section 7 of the application):\n\n  - Permit set complete: 08/2025\n  - Construction start: 10/2025\n  - Mechanical completion: 02/2026\n  - Ready for witness test: 03/2026\n\nIf any of those dates look unworkable against your screening or study calendar, please tell us now rather than later — we would much rather adjust on the front end than discover a slip in September. I am reachable at the number below any weekday, and Meera has my mobile if something needs a faster turn.\n\nThank you for the continued partnership. We appreciate the DER Program Office's attention on this one — it is a visible project for the City and the Council is watching the schedule closely.\n\nBest regards,\n\nBill Tran\nEnergy Manager\nCity of Elmsworth\n300 City Center Way\nElmsworth, Alleron 07EL\n(612) 236-0402\nbill.tran@cityofelmsworth.gov\n\nAttachments:\n  - PXA-2025-0198_Elmsworth_Application.pdf (Form DIS-APP-01, 4 pp.)	<h1 id="2025-05-22-elmsworth-cover-email">2025-05-22 Elmsworth Cover Email</h1>\n<p><strong>From:</strong> Bill Tran <a href="&#109;&#97;&#105;&#108;&#116;&#111;&#58;&#98;&#105;&#108;&#108;&#46;&#116;&#114;&#97;&#110;&#64;&#99;&#105;&#116;&#121;&#111;&#102;&#101;&#108;&#109;&#115;&#119;&#111;&#114;&#116;&#104;&#46;&#103;&#111;&#118;">&#98;&#105;&#108;&#108;&#46;&#116;&#114;&#97;&#110;&#64;&#99;&#105;&#116;&#121;&#111;&#102;&#101;&#108;&#109;&#115;&#119;&#111;&#114;&#116;&#104;&#46;&#103;&#111;&#118;</a><br>\n<strong>To:</strong> DER Program Office <a href="&#109;&#97;&#105;&#108;&#116;&#111;&#58;&#100;&#101;&#114;&#46;&#112;&#114;&#111;&#103;&#114;&#97;&#109;&#64;&#97;&#108;&#108;&#101;&#110;&#105;&#111;&#109;&#46;&#99;&#111;&#109;">&#100;&#101;&#114;&#46;&#112;&#114;&#111;&#103;&#114;&#97;&#109;&#64;&#97;&#108;&#108;&#101;&#110;&#105;&#111;&#109;&#46;&#99;&#111;&#109;</a><br>\n<strong>Date:</strong> Thu, 22 May 2025 10:47:22 -0500<br>\n<strong>Subject:</strong> PXA-2025-0198 submission — Municipal Service Center PV<br>\n<strong>Cc:</strong> Meera Vellanki <a href="&#109;&#97;&#105;&#108;&#116;&#111;&#58;&#109;&#101;&#101;&#114;&#97;&#46;&#118;&#101;&#108;&#108;&#97;&#110;&#107;&#105;&#64;&#97;&#108;&#108;&#101;&#110;&#105;&#111;&#109;&#46;&#99;&#111;&#109;">&#109;&#101;&#101;&#114;&#97;&#46;&#118;&#101;&#108;&#108;&#97;&#110;&#107;&#105;&#64;&#97;&#108;&#108;&#101;&#110;&#105;&#111;&#109;&#46;&#99;&#111;&#109;</a></p>\n<hr>\n<p>DER Program Office —</p>\n<p>Attached please find the City of Elmsworth's DER interconnection application for the Municipal Service Center PV project (Form DIS-APP-01), assigned Application ID PXA-2025-0198 on your intake page. Nameplate is 900 kW AC, behind-the-meter with export capability, mounted on the Municipal Service Center rooftop and adjacent parking canopy.</p>\n<p>For your records, this filing follows our earlier application PXA-2023-0412 dated 04/12/2023 for the same Municipal Service Center site. The 2023 filing sat with our office through a budget cycle change and a facilities director turnover on our side, and we did not push it forward during that period. The scope in the current package is materially the same site, the same 900 kW envelope, and the same point of interconnection area on the mid-town Elmsworth feeder — the update is the CEL-2025-Q2 inverter selection and refreshed drawings dated 05/16/2025.</p>\n<p>Given the continuity of the project, we would like to retain our original 2023 queue position. Council approved the capital allocation in the FY25 budget on the assumption that we would be in construction this fall, and every month we slide back in the queue is a month that pushes mechanical completion past the winter shutdown window and into next spring. We would appreciate your team's confirmation on that point at your earliest convenience so we can lock in permit and procurement dates.</p>\n<p>We are targeting the following applicant-side milestones (also carried in Section 7 of the application):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Permit set complete: 08/2025</li>\n<li>Construction start: 10/2025</li>\n<li>Mechanical completion: 02/2026</li>\n<li>Ready for witness test: 03/2026</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If any of those dates look unworkable against your screening or study calendar, please tell us now rather than later — we would much rather adjust on the front end than discover a slip in September. I am reachable at the number below any weekday, and Meera has my mobile if something needs a faster turn.</p>\n<p>Thank you for the continued partnership. We appreciate the DER Program Office's attention on this one — it is a visible project for the City and the Council is watching the schedule closely.</p>\n<p>Best regards,</p>\n<p>Bill Tran<br>\nEnergy Manager<br>\nCity of Elmsworth<br>\n300 City Center Way<br>\nElmsworth, Alleron 07EL<br>\n(612) 236-0402<br>\nbill.tran@cityofelmsworth.gov</p>\n<p>Attachments:<br>\n  - PXA-2025-0198_Elmsworth_Application.pdf (Form DIS-APP-01, 4 pp.)</p>	[]	markdown	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	markdown	en	15	15	{}
2	der-program/applications/pxa-2023-0412-elmsworth	73ec153dee747002b948	PXA-2023-0412 Elmsworth	Original application PXA-2023-0412 filed 04/12/2023 for the Elmsworth municipal service center	f	t				# PXA-2023-0412 Elmsworth\n\nAlleniom Utilities — DER Program Office · Form DER-APP-01 PXA-2023-0412 · Page 1\nALLENIOM UTILITIES\nDER Program Office (612) 555-0100  ·  alleniom.com\nder.program@alleniom.com\nCOMMERCIAL DISTRIBUTED ENERGY RESOURCE\nINTERCONNECTION APPLICATION\nForm DER-APP-01  ·  Program Scope: ≥500 kW\nApplication ID\nFiled\nReceived by\nApplication Class\nInterconnection Category\nProgram office use only — queue date\nSection 1 — Applicant Information\nLegal name of applicant\nEntity type\nApplicant address\nMain phone\nPrimary contact\nContact email\nContact phone\nAuthorized signatory\nElectric account holder\nAlleniom account number\nSection 2 — Site Information\nSite name\nSite address\nParcel ID\nExisting utility service\nExisting on-site DER\nHost meter number\nSite occupancy\nRoof type / mounting\nSection 3 — Facility Description\nThe proposed distributed energy resource is a rooftop photovoltaic generating facility installed across the two principal\nbuildings of the Municipal Service Center (Building A — fleet maintenance; Building B — public works administration\nand storage). The array will operate behind the customer's revenue meter, offsetting site load with export permitted during\nperiods when generation exceeds coincident on-site demand.\n4200 Veldmere Boulevard, Halston, Alleron 01HA\n\n---\n\nAlleniom Utilities — DER Program Office · Form DER-APP-01 PXA-2023-0412 · Page 2\nGenerator type\nPrime mover\nAggregate nameplate capacity\nDC array capacity\nOperating voltage (POI)\nExport mode\nIslanding\nAnti-islanding basis\nSection 4 — Equipment Schedule\nPV Modules\nItem Description Quantity Unit Rating\nAggreg\nate DC\nInverters\nItem Description Qty Unit (kW AC) Aggregate (kW\nAC)\nBalance-of-System\nItem\n4.3\n4.4\n4.5\n4.6\n4.7\n4.8\n4.9\nProtection & Controls\nItem\n4.10\n4.11\n4.12\nTelemetry / Communications\nItem\n4.13\n4.14 Provision for utility-owned RTU and SCADA telemetry at electrical room — conduit, backboard space, dedicated 120 V\ncircuit, and hand-off point per Alleniom Telemetry & Communications Standard (equipment to be furnished by Alleniom)\n\n---\n\nAlleniom Utilities — DER Program Office · Form DER-APP-01 PXA-2023-0412 · Page 3\nSection 5 — Point of Interconnection\nFeeder / circuit  (Elmsworth Substation, Bus 2)\nService transformer 1,500 kVA pad-mount, 12.47 kV — 480Y/277 V (utility-owned)\nDistance from POI to first PV\ncombiner (approx.)\n190 ft\nExisting service capacity 1,600 A main\nRequested export limit None (up to nameplate)\nAnticipated in-service date Q4 2023 (subject to study and construction scheduling)\nSection 7 — Applicant Certification\nThe undersigned certifies that the information provided on this application and its attachments is true and correct to the\nbest of the applicant's knowledge, that the proposed facility will be installed and operated in conformance with applicable\nAlleniom Utilities interconnection standards and the National Electrical Code, and that the applicant will cooperate in the\nexchange of engineering information required to complete technical screening, any applicable studies, and commissioning\nof the facility.\nSignature\nPrinted name\nTitle\nOrganization\nDate\nALN-306\nSection 6 - Application Fee\nInterconnection request fee (check no. 21188, $2,500.00) was received 04/10/2023 and is recorded in Alleniom's\npayments ledger.\n\n---\n\nAlleniom Utilities — DER Program Office · Form DER-APP-01 PXA-2023-0412 · Page 4\nProgram Office Intake Stamp\nReceived\nAssigned ID\nAssigned to\nFee received\nCompleteness check\nScreening start\n\n---\n\nAlleniom Utilities — DER Program Office · Form DER-APP-01 PXA-2023-0412 · Page 5\nFile Notes / Correspondence Log\nApplication: PXA-2023-0412 — City of Elmsworth — Municipal Service Center (900 kW rooftop PV)\nLog maintained by: DER Program Office · Interconnection Studies\nAll entries recorded on receipt or on transmittal; times omitted. Blank rows indicate no correspondence or file activity recorded for the\nperiod.\nDate Dir. Party Channel Subject / Notes\nAcknowledgment of receipt sent to B. Tran; ID\nPXA-2023-0412 assigned; screening desk assignment noted.\nInitial screening comments — request for updated single-line\nindicating fault-current contribution basis; request for\nclarification of intended export operating mode.\nScreening follow-up: request for confirmation of\nConfirmation of disconnect location per site plan Sheet 1;\nstructural letter update forthcoming.\nReminder — structural letter update outstanding; also\nrequested confirmation of anticipated in-service date given\nscreening progress.\nSecond reminder — structural letter update; noted that\nadditional review comments would follow once the packet is\ncomplete.\nRoutine information response — acknowledged outstanding\nitems and indicated the city was coordinating internally on the\nstructural update and revised schedule; no attachments\nprovided.\nutility-accessible disconnect location and preliminary\nstructural letter update.\n\n---\n\nAlleniom Utilities — DER Program Office · Form DER-APP-01 PXA-2023-0412 · Page 6\nDate Dir. Party Channel Subject / Notes\nEnd of file — PXA-2023-0412	<h1 id="pxa-2023-0412-elmsworth">PXA-2023-0412 Elmsworth</h1>\n<p>Alleniom Utilities — DER Program Office · Form DER-APP-01 PXA-2023-0412 · Page 1<br>\nALLENIOM UTILITIES<br>\nDER Program Office (612) 555-0100  ·  alleniom.com<br>\nder.program@alleniom.com<br>\nCOMMERCIAL DISTRIBUTED ENERGY RESOURCE<br>\nINTERCONNECTION APPLICATION<br>\nForm DER-APP-01  ·  Program Scope: ≥500 kW<br>\nApplication ID<br>\nFiled<br>\nReceived by<br>\nApplication Class<br>\nInterconnection Category<br>\nProgram office use only — queue date<br>\nSection 1 — Applicant Information<br>\nLegal name of applicant<br>\nEntity type<br