5	der-program/applications/pxa-2025-0231-inverter-spec-sheets	79d37066d9c635b27ab1	PXA-2025-0231 Inverter Spec Sheets	Manufacturer datasheets for PXA-2025-0231 inverters with nameplate ratings summing to 750 kW	f	t				# PXA-2025-0231 Inverter Spec Sheets\n\nPXA-2025-0231 — Inverter Nameplate & Spec Sheets Compiled 06/09/2025 — Karsten Solar Development LLC\nPage 1 Doc PXA-2025-0231-INV Rev 0\nInverter Nameplate & Spec Sheets\nPXA-2025-0231\nFiled as companion file to Application PXA-2025-0231 — Wexley Distribution Center, Halston Regional\nCross-Dock\nCompiled by: Karsten Solar Development LLC · Emery Traskin, Development Manager\nCompilation date: 06/09/2025\nContents: Manufacturer-published product datasheets for the commercial three-phase string inverters listed in\nSection 4.1 of Application PXA-2025-0231.\nCompilation Index\nItem Manufacturer Model Nameplate AC Output Qty\nINV-1 Solmery Power SM-125K-3P 125 kW 1 unit\nINV-2 Solmery Power SM-125K-3P 125 kW 1 unit\nINV-3 Solmery Power SM-125K-3P 125 kW 1 unit\nINV-4 Torvane Electric TE-125K 125 kW 1 unit\nINV-5 Torvane Electric TE-125K 125 kW 1 unit\nINV-6 Torvane Electric TE-125K 125 kW 1 unit\nAggregate inverter nameplate AC output on PXA-2025-0231: 750 kW (six units of 125 kW nameplate each, as\nrecorded on the manufacturer datasheets that follow).\nThe following inverter nameplate and certification data are summarized below:\nTwo inverter model summary sheets follow - one per inverter model - presenting the nameplate ratings and\ncertification-relevant specifications, compiled by the applicant's engineer from manufacturer product\nliterature current as of the filing date.\n\n---\n\nPXA-2025-0231 — Inverter Nameplate & Spec Sheets\nCompiled 06/09/2025 — Karsten Solar Development LLC\nPage 2\nDoc PXA-2025-0231-INV Rev 0\nDatasheet 1 — Solmery Power SM-125K-3P\nSolmery Power, Inc.\nCommercial Three-Phase String Inverter Product Line\nDatasheet Ref. SM-125K-3P · Document DS-SM125-R7 · Publication date 02/2025\nSolmery Power, Inc. · 1900 Highfield Industrial Drive · Aurora, Illinois 60506 · United States\nProduct Support: (630) 555-0182 · support@solmerypower.com · solmerypower.com\nProduct Description\nThe Solmery Power SM-125K-3P is a transformerless, three-phase commercial string inverter engineered for\nbehind-the-meter and front-of-the-meter commercial and industrial photovoltaic installations. The unit is intended\nfor outdoor pad-mount or wall-mount deployment and is designed for 480 V wye grid interconnection on\nsecondary distribution systems.\nNameplate — AC Output\nNameplate AC output power (continuous, rated)\n125 kW\nNameplate AC output power (peak, ≤10 s)\n130 kW\nNominal AC output voltage\n480 V, 3-phase, 4-wire (wye) + PE\nAC output voltage operating range\n422 V – 528 V (–12 % / +10 %)\nNominal output frequency\n60 Hz\nOutput frequency operating range\n57.0 – 62.0 Hz (adjustable per utility)\nNominal AC output current, continuous\n150.4 A per phase\nMaximum AC output current\n156.4 A per phase\nPower factor at rated power\nUnity (adjustable 0.80 leading – 0.80 lagging)\nTotal harmonic distortion (current, at rated output)\n< 3 %\nInrush current\n< 20 A peak\nUtility interconnection topology\nThree-phase, four-wire, transformerless\nDC Input\nMaximum recommended PV field DC input power\n187.5 kW (1.50× DC/AC)\nAbsolute maximum DC input voltage (Voc, cold)\n1,100 V DC\nMPPT voltage range, full-power\n550 V – 950 V DC\nMPPT voltage range, operating\n200 V – 1,000 V DC\nStartup DC voltage\n250 V DC\nNumber of independent MPP trackers\n6\nDC inputs per MPPT\n4 (24 total; fused positive and negative)\nMaximum input current per MPPT\n40 A\nMaximum short-circuit input current per MPPT\n60 A\nReverse polarity protection\nYes (integrated)\nIntegrated DC disconnect\nYes, load-break rated\nType II surge protection (DC side)\nYes, integrated\n\n\n---\n\nPXA-2025-0231 — Inverter Nameplate & Spec Sheets Compiled 06/09/2025 — Karsten Solar Development LLC\nPage 3 Doc PXA-2025-0231-INV Rev 0\nSolmery Power SM-125K-3P (continued)\nEfficiency\nPeak conversion efficiency 98.6 %\nCEC weighted efficiency 98.3 %\nEuropean weighted efficiency 98.2 %\nEfficiency at 25 % of rated output (600 V DC) 97.4 %\nEfficiency at 50 % of rated output (600 V DC) 98.3 %\nEfficiency at 75 % of rated output (600 V DC) 98.5 %\nEfficiency at 100 % of rated output (600 V DC) 98.4 %\nEfficiency curve (nominal, MPP voltage = 600 V DC):\n     %\n  99 |\n     |                      ●●●●●●\n  98 |               ●●●●●●●     ●●●●\n     |         ●●●●●●\n  97 |     ●●●●\n     |   ●●\n  96 | ●●\n     |●\n  95 +■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■→\n     0  10   25   50   75   100  %  (fraction of nameplate AC output)\nGrid Support / Interoperability\nAnti-islanding Passive + active; IEEE 1547-2018 § 8.2 compliant\nVolt-VAR / Volt-Watt / Frequency-Watt Supported; utility-configurable\nCommunications Modbus TCP, SunSpec Modbus, DNP3 (optional)\nSite controller compatibility Solmery SP-Link (optional plant controller — sold\nseparately; not included with unit)\nEfficiency curve figures are indicative; the certified efficiency measurement was performed under ISO 17025-accredited\ntesting laboratory conditions.\n\n---\n\nPXA-2025-0231 — Inverter Nameplate & Spec Sheets Compiled 06/09/2025 — Karsten Solar Development LLC\nPage 4 Doc PXA-2025-0231-INV Rev 0\nSolmery Power SM-125K-3P (continued)\nEnvironmental / Mechanical\nAmbient operating temperature –30 °C to +60 °C (derating above +45 °C)\nStorage temperature –40 °C to +70 °C\nRelative humidity 0 – 100 %, condensing\nCooling Forced air, temperature-controlled variable-speed\nfans\nEnclosure rating Type 4X (IP66)\nAltitude, no derating Up to 2,000 m; derated above 2,000 m\nDimensions (H × W × D) 1,050 × 720 × 360 mm\nWeight 92 kg\nAudible noise at 1 m < 65 dB(A)\nStandard Listings & Certifications\nThe SM-125K-3P has been evaluated to the following standards. Certification marks reflect the base listings\ncurrently held by the product family.\n  UL 1741-SB — Grid Support Utility Interactive Inverters and Converters (base listing; supplement SB, dated\n09/2021)\n  UL 1741 — Standard for Inverters, Converters, Controllers, and Interconnection System Equipment for Use with\nDistributed Energy Resources\n  IEEE 1547-2018 — Interconnection and Interoperability of Distributed Energy Resources with Associated\nElectric Power Systems Interfaces\n  IEEE 1547.1-2020 — Conformance Test Procedures for Equipment Interconnecting Distributed Energy\nResources with Electric Power Systems\n  CSA C22.2 No. 107.1-16\n  FCC Part 15, Class A (emissions)\n  IEC 62109-1 and IEC 62109-2 (product safety)\nThe base UL 1741-SB listing evaluates the inverter as a grid-support utility-interactive inverter to the requirements\nof Supplement SB (grid-support functions). The base listing does not, in itself, evaluate the unit against\nSupplement SB Power Control System (PCS) mode; the PCS-mode evaluation under Supplement SB is a\nseparate, additional certification and is not held by the SM-125K-3P as listed above. The product family has not\nbeen evaluated to UL 3141 (Power Control Systems).\nWarranty\n10-year standard product warranty on the inverter; 20-year extended warranty available.\n\n---\n\nPXA-2025-0231 — Inverter Nameplate & Spec Sheets\nCompiled 06/09/2025 — Karsten Solar Development LLC\nPage 5\nDoc PXA-2025-0231-INV Rev 0\nDatasheet 2 — Torvane Electric TE-125K\nTorvane Electric Corporation\nCommercial PV Inverter Division\nDatasheet Ref. TE-125K · Document DTS-TE125-Rev4 · Publication date 11/2024\nTorvane Electric Corporation · 2440 Merlan Way, Building 4 · Beaverton, Oregon 97006 · United States\nTechnical Support: (503) 555-0219 · techsupport@torvane-electric.com · torvane-electric.com\nProduct Description\nThe Torvane Electric TE-125K is a commercial-grade transformerless three-phase string inverter for grid-parallel\nphotovoltaic generation. The TE-125K is designed for 480 V wye distribution interconnection and is suitable for\nbehind-the-meter industrial and commercial PV plants. The unit is a natural evolution of the TE-100K platform,\nsharing its power stage topology with an uprated output stage.\nNameplate — AC Output\nNameplate AC output power (continuous)\n125 kW\nMaximum AC output power (short-term, 10 s)\n132 kW\nNominal AC output voltage\n480 V, 3-phase, 4-wire (wye + neutral)\nAC voltage operating band\n422 V – 528 V\nNominal AC frequency\n60 Hz\nFrequency operating band\n57.0 – 62.0 Hz\nContinuous AC output current\n150.4 A per phase\nMaximum AC output current\n158.8 A per phase\nPower factor\nUnity nominal; adjustable 0.80 lead / 0.80 lag\nCurrent THD at rated output\n< 3.0 %\nGrid connection type\nThree-phase, four-wire + PE (wye)\nUtility isolation\nNon-isolated (transformerless)\n\n\n---\n\nPXA-2025-0231 — Inverter Nameplate & Spec Sheets\nCompiled 06/09/2025 — Karsten Solar Development LLC\nPage 6\nDoc PXA-2025-0231-INV Rev 0\nDC Input\nRecommended maximum PV field size (DC)\n175 kW (up to 1.40× DC/AC recommended; 1.50×\npermitted)\nAbsolute maximum DC voltage (open-circuit, cold)\n1,100 V DC\nMPPT operating range (full power)\n570 V – 950 V DC\nMPPT full range\n200 V – 1,000 V DC\nStartup DC voltage\n260 V DC\nNumber of MPP trackers\n8\nDC string inputs per MPPT\n3 (24 total)\nMaximum current per MPPT\n32 A\nMaximum short-circuit current per MPPT\n45 A\nDC input protection\nIntegrated string fusing (positive + negative); polarity\nreverse protection\nIntegrated DC load-break disconnect\nYes\nDC surge protection\nType II, integrated\n\n\n---\n\nPXA-2025-0231 — Inverter Nameplate & Spec Sheets Compiled 06/09/2025 — Karsten Solar Development LLC\nPage 7 Doc PXA-2025-0231-INV Rev 0\nTorvane Electric TE-125K (continued)\nEfficiency\nPeak conversion efficiency 98.5 %\nCEC weighted efficiency 98.1 %\nEuropean weighted efficiency 98.0 %\nEfficiency at 20 % of nameplate output 96.9 %\nEfficiency at 50 % of nameplate output 98.2 %\nEfficiency at 75 % of nameplate output 98.4 %\nEfficiency at 100 % of nameplate output 98.3 %\nEfficiency curve (nominal, MPP voltage = 620 V DC):\n     %\n  99 |\n     |                    ●●●●●●●\n  98 |             ●●●●●●●       ●●●\n     |         ●●●●\n  97 |     ●●●●\n     |   ●●\n  96 |●●●\n     |●\n  95 +■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■→\n     0  10   20   50   75   100  %  (fraction of nameplate output)\nGrid Support / Interoperability\nAnti-islanding Active + passive, IEEE 1547-2018 § 8.2 compliant\nVolt-VAR, Volt-Watt, Freq-Watt, Constant PF Supported and utility-programmable\nCommunications Modbus RTU (RS-485), Modbus TCP (Ethernet),\nSunSpec\nOptional plant controller Torvane TE-PC-1000 plant controller (external\naccessory, sold separately; not included)\nCurve values are indicative of nominal operation at 620 V DC input; certified measurement points were recorded under\naccredited test-laboratory conditions.\n\n---\n\nPXA-2025-0231 — Inverter Nameplate & Spec Sheets Compiled 06/09/2025 — Karsten Solar Development LLC\nPage 8 Doc PXA-2025-0231-INV Rev 0\nTorvane Electric TE-125K (continued)\nEnvironmental / Mechanical\nOperating ambient temperature –25 °C to +60 °C (derating above +50 °C)\nStorage temperature –40 °C to +70 °C\nRelative humidity 0 – 100 % condensing\nCooling Forced convection, variable-speed fans\nEnclosure rating Type 4X (IP66)\nAltitude (no derating) Up to 2,000 m\nDimensions (H × W × D) 1,075 × 700 × 370 mm\nWeight 88 kg\nAudible noise at 1 m < 65 dB(A)\nStandard Listings & Certifications\nThe TE-125K holds the following standard listings as evaluated by a Nationally Recognized Testing Laboratory\n(NRTL).\n  UL 1741-SB — Inverters, Converters, Controllers and Interconnection System Equipment for Use With\nDistributed Energy Resources (base listing to Supplement SB, evaluated to grid-support utility-interactive\nrequirements)\n  UL 1741 — parent standard\n  IEEE 1547-2018 — DER interconnection and interoperability\n  IEEE 1547.1-2020 — conformance test procedures\n  CSA C22.2 No. 107.1-16\n  FCC Part 15, Subpart B, Class A\n  IEC 62109-1 / IEC 62109-2 — product safety\nThe TE-125K's UL 1741-SB listing evaluates the unit as a grid-support utility-interactive inverter under\nSupplement SB. The base Supplement SB listing does not include an evaluation to Supplement SB's Power\nControl System mode; that mode is a separate, additional evaluation and is not carried by the TE-125K. The\nTE-125K product family is not evaluated to UL 3141.\nWarranty\nStandard 10-year product warranty. Extended 20-year and 25-year warranty tiers available.\n\n---\n\nPXA-2025-0231 — Inverter Nameplate & Spec Sheets Compiled 06/09/2025 — Karsten Solar Development LLC\nPage 9 Doc PXA-2025-0231-INV Rev 0\nCompilation Footer\n  Solmery Power SM-125K-3P — 125 kW nameplate AC output (three units on this project)\n  Torvane Electric TE-125K — 125 kW nameplate AC output (three units on this project)\nSum of unit nameplate AC output ratings across the six inverters listed in Section 4.1 of the Application: 125 kW +\n125 kW + 125 kW + 125 kW + 125 kW + 125 kW = 750 kW.\nFiled by: Karsten Solar Development LLC · Emery Traskin, Development Manager · 3115 Larkspur Court, Suite 210, Halston, Alleron\nDoc no. PXA-2025-0231-INV · Rev 0 · 06/09/2025 · Applicant: Wexley Distribution Center (Developer of Record: Karsten Solar\nDevelopment LLC)\nThis compilation summarizes nameplate and certification data for the inverter equipment scheduled in\nSection 4.1 of Application PXA-2025-0231, compiled by the applicant from manufacturer product literature.\n07HA · (612) 555-1642 · emery.traskin@karstensolar.com	<h1 id="pxa-2025-0231-inverter-spec-sheets">PXA-2025-0231 Inverter Spec Sheets</h1>\n<p>PXA-2025-0231 — Inverter Nameplate &amp; Spec Sheets Compiled 06/09/2025 — Karsten Solar Development LLC<br>\nPage 1 Doc PXA-2025-0231-INV Rev 0<br>\nInverter Nameplate &amp; Spec Sheets<br>\nPXA-2025-0231<br>\nFiled as companion file to Application PXA-2025-0231 — 