c TE-125K is a commercial-grade transformerless three-phase string inverter for grid-parallel<br>\nphotovoltaic generation. The TE-125K is designed for 480 V wye distribution interconnection and is suitable for<br>\nbehind-the-meter industrial and commercial PV plants. The unit is a natural evolution of the TE-100K platform,<br>\nsharing its power stage topology with an uprated output stage.<br>\nNameplate — AC Output<br>\nNameplate AC output power (continuous)<br>\n125 kW<br>\nMaximum AC output power (short-term, 10 s)<br>\n132 kW<br>\nNominal AC output voltage<br>\n480 V, 3-phase, 4-wire (wye + neutral)<br>\nAC voltage operating band<br>\n422 V – 528 V<br>\nNominal AC frequency<br>\n60 Hz<br>\nFrequency operating band<br>\n57.0 – 62.0 Hz<br>\nContinuous AC output current<br>\n150.4 A per phase<br>\nMaximum AC output current<br>\n158.8 A per phase<br>\nPower factor<br>\nUnity nominal; adjustable 0.80 lead / 0.80 lag<br>\nCurrent THD at rated output<br>\n&lt; 3.0 %<br>\nGrid connection type<br>\nThree-phase, four-wire + PE (wye)<br>\nUtility isolation<br>\nNon-isolated (transformerless)</p>\n<hr>\n<p>PXA-2025-0231 — Inverter Nameplate &amp; Spec Sheets<br>\nCompiled 06/09/2025 — Karsten Solar Development LLC<br>\nPage 6<br>\nDoc PXA-2025-0231-INV Rev 0<br>\nDC Input<br>\nRecommended maximum PV field size (DC)<br>\n175 kW (up to 1.40× DC/AC recommended; 1.50×<br>\npermitted)<br>\nAbsolute maximum DC voltage (open-circuit, cold)<br>\n1,100 V DC<br>\nMPPT operating range (full power)<br>\n570 V – 950 V DC<br>\nMPPT full range<br>\n200 V – 1,000 V DC<br>\nStartup DC voltage<br>\n260 V DC<br>\nNumber of MPP trackers<br>\n8<br>\nDC string inputs per MPPT<br>\n3 (24 total)<br>\nMaximum current per MPPT<br>\n32 A<br>\nMaximum short-circuit current per MPPT<br>\n45 A<br>\nDC input protection<br>\nIntegrated string fusing (positive + negative); polarity<br>\nreverse protection<br>\nIntegrated DC load-break disconnect<br>\nYes<br>\nDC surge protection<br>\nType II, integrated</p>\n<hr>\n<p>PXA-2025-0231 — Inverter Nameplate &amp; Spec Sheets Compiled 06/09/2025 — Karsten Solar Development LLC<br>\nPage 7 Doc PXA-2025-0231-INV Rev 0<br>\nTorvane Electric TE-125K (continued)<br>\nEfficiency<br>\nPeak conversion efficiency 98.5 %<br>\nCEC weighted efficiency 98.1 %<br>\nEuropean weighted efficiency 98.0 %<br>\nEfficiency at 20 % of nameplate output 96.9 %<br>\nEfficiency at 50 % of nameplate output 98.2 %<br>\nEfficiency at 75 % of nameplate output 98.4 %<br>\nEfficiency at 100 % of nameplate output 98.3 %<br>\nEfficiency curve (nominal, MPP voltage = 620 V DC):<br>\n     %<br>\n  99 |<br>\n     |                    ●●●●●●●<br>\n  98 |             ●●●●●●●       ●●●<br>\n     |         ●●●●<br>\n  97 |     ●●●●<br>\n     |   ●●<br>\n  96 |●●●<br>\n     |●<br>\n  95 +■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■■→<br>\n     0  10   20   50   75   100  %  (fraction of nameplate output)<br>\nGrid Support / Interoperability<br>\nAnti-islanding Active + passive, IEEE 1547-2018 § 8.2 compliant<br>\nVolt-VAR, Volt-Watt, Freq-Watt, Constant PF Supported and utility-programmable<br>\nCommunications Modbus RTU (RS-485), Modbus TCP (Ethernet),<br>\nSunSpec<br>\nOptional plant controller Torvane TE-PC-1000 plant controller (external<br>\naccessory, sold separately; not included)<br>\nCurve values are indicative of nominal operation at 620 V DC input; certified measurement points were recorded under<br>\naccredited test-laboratory conditions.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>PXA-2025-0231 — Inverter Nameplate &amp; Spec Sheets Compiled 06/09/2025 — Karsten Solar Development LLC<br>\nPage 8 Doc PXA-2025-0231-INV Rev 0<br>\nTorvane Electric TE-125K (continued)<br>\nEnvironmental / Mechanical<br>\nOperating ambient temperature –25 °C to +60 °C (derating above +50 °C)<br>\nStorage temperature –40 °C to +70 °C<br>\nRelative humidity 0 – 100 % condensing<br>\nCooling Forced convection, variable-speed fans<br>\nEnclosure rating Type 4X (IP66)<br>\nAltitude (no derating) Up to 2,000 m<br>\nDimensions (H × W × D) 1,075 × 700 × 370 mm<br>\nWeight 88 kg<br>\nAudible noise at 1 m &lt; 65 dB(A)<br>\nStandard Listings &amp; Certifications<br>\nThe TE-125K holds the following standard listings as evaluated by a Nationally Recognized Testing Laboratory<br>\n(NRTL).<br>\n  UL 1741-SB — Inverters, Converters, Controllers and Interconnection System Equipment for Use With<br>\nDistributed Energy Resources (base listing to Supplement SB, evaluated to grid-support utility-interactive<br>\nrequirements)<br>\n  UL 1741 — parent standard<br>\n  IEEE 1547-2018 — DER interconnection and interoperability<br>\n  IEEE 1547.1-2020 — conformance test procedures<br>\n  CSA C22.2 No. 107.1-16<br>\n  FCC Part 15, Subpart B, Class A<br>\n  IEC 62109-1 / IEC 62109-2 — product safety<br>\nThe TE-125K's UL 1741-SB listing evaluates the unit as a grid-support utility-interactive inverter under<br>\nSupplement SB. The base Supplement SB listing does not include an evaluation to Supplement SB's Power<br>\nControl System mode; that mode is a separate, additional evaluation and is not carried by the TE-125K. The<br>\nTE-125K product family is not evaluated to UL 3141.<br>\nWarranty<br>\nStandard 10-year product warranty. Extended 20-year and 25-year warranty tiers available.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>PXA-2025-0231 — Inverter Nameplate &amp; Spec Sheets Compiled 06/09/2025 — Karsten Solar Development LLC<br>\nPage 9 Doc PXA-2025-0231-INV Rev 0<br>\nCompilation Footer<br>\n  Solmery Power SM-125K-3P — 125 kW nameplate AC output (three units on this project)<br>\n  Torvane Electric TE-125K — 125 kW nameplate AC output (three units on this project)<br>\nSum of unit nameplate AC output ratings across the six inverters listed in Section 4.1 of the Application: 125 kW +<br>\n125 kW + 125 kW + 125 kW + 125 kW + 125 kW = 750 kW.<br>\nFiled by: Karsten Solar Development LLC · Emery Traskin, Development Manager · 3115 Larkspur Court, Suite 210, Halston, Alleron<br>\nDoc no. PXA-2025-0231-INV · Rev 0 · 06/09/2025 · Applicant: Wexley Distribution Center (Developer of Record: Karsten Solar<br>\nDevelopment LLC)<br>\nThis compilation summarizes nameplate and certification data for the inverter equipment scheduled in<br>\nSection 4.1 of Application PXA-2025-0231, compiled by the applicant from manufacturer product literature.<br>\n07HA · (612) 555-1642 · emery.traskin@karstensolar.com</p>	[]	markdown	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	markdown	en	31	31	{}
6	der-program/applications/pxa-2025-0231-stated-480kw	73bcbf6c5f827bd2159e	PXA-2025-0231 Stated 480kW	Application PXA-2025-0231 stating capacity 480 kW with export-limited operation claim	f	t				# PXA-2025-0231 Stated 480kW\n\nALLENIOM UTILITIES — DER PROGRAM OFFICE\nDER INTERCONNECTION APPLICATION (COMMERCIAL, ≥ 500\nkW)\nForm DIS-APP-01 · governed by DIS-01 Rev 4 · Alleniom DER Interconnection Standard\nApplication ID: PXA-2025-0231\nReceived (utility use only)\nApplication version\nFiling category\nProcessing track requested\nSection 1 — Applicant Information\nApplicant / interconnection\ncustomer\nEntity type\nCustomer mailing address\nCustomer site contact\nCustomer site phone\nCustomer site email\nDeveloper of record (preparer\n& filer)\nDeveloper mailing address\nDeveloper primary contact\nDeveloper phone\nDeveloper email\nSigning authority for this\nfiling\nEmery Traskin, Development Manager, Karsten Solar Development LLC (as\nauthorized agent of Wexley Distribution Center)\nThe Developer of Record certifies that it has been retained by Wexley Distribution Center — the customer\nof record on the retail electric account serving the facility identified in Section 2 — and is authorized to\nsubmit this Application and to correspond with Alleniom Utilities on the customer's behalf regarding all\nmatters of interconnection.\nSection 2 — Site Information\nFacility name\nService address\nFacility use\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0231  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 1\n\n---\n\nRetail rate class\nExisting electric service\nExisting utility meter\nSite ownership\nAssigned distribution feeder\n(per pre-application review)\nSubstation\nFacility peak demand (last 12\nmonths, billed)\nFacility minimum demand\n(24/7 refrigerated and staging\nload)\nOperating schedule\nBackup generation on site\nSection 3 — Proposed DER\nDER technology\nProject description Behind-the-meter ground-mount PV array with parking-lot carport PV addition,\nserving warehouse load with limited export\nStated capacity\nMounting\nFuel / energy source\nOperating mode requested Parallel operation with utility service; export limited to the Stated Capacity\nabove via inverter power-control settings\nExpected export\nAnticipated in-service\n3.1 Capacity Basis Statement (from Applicant)\nThe Applicant proposes to operate this DER facility at a Stated Capacity of 480 kW — export-limited\noperation at the point of common coupling. Output is constrained through the on-site inverter fleet's\nprogrammable power-control settings, which the Developer will configure at commissioning to cap\nreal-power delivery at the point of common coupling to the stated 480 kW value under all operating\nconditions. On this basis the Applicant requests the Application be reviewed at the stated 480 kW figure.\nSection 4 — Point of Interconnection\nPoint of interconnection New 800 A, 3-phase back-fed breaker in the existing 480 V main distribution\nswitchboard (MDS-1) in the warehouse main electrical room\nDistance from PV combiner to\nPOI\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0231  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 2\n\n---\n\nPoint of common coupling\nFeeder assignment\nShared POI request (DIS-01\n§3.5)\n4.1 Connection Description\nThe proposed PV system ties into the customer-owned side of the site's existing electrical service. Power\nflow from the six commercial three-phase inverters (see the companion inverter datasheets file for per-unit\nratings) is aggregated at PVC-1, routed through the pad-mount lockable AC disconnect (PVD-1), and\nlands on a new 800 A back-fed breaker in MDS-1. MDS-1 is fed from the plant's existing utility service\ntransformer through the site's existing 480 V main service disconnect and the existing utility revenue\nmeter.\nThe new PV interconnection is behind the existing service meter — the same point of common coupling\nas the site's existing electrical service — on the load side of the utility revenue meter and upstream of the\nwarehouse's process and refrigeration load buses.\nNo new utility-side equipment, no new service transformer, no new service drop, and no separate revenue\nmeter is requested. The Applicant proposes to net the PV generation against warehouse load through the\nexisting bidirectional revenue meter of record and to hold export at the point of common coupling to the\nStated Capacity of 480 kW under all operating conditions.\nSection 5 — Equipment Schedule\nThe proposed facility uses a fleet of commercial three-phase string inverters. Individual inverter nameplate\nratings, model-level specifications, and manufacturer certifications are provided in the companion file\nInverter Nameplate & Spec Sheets — PXA-2025-0231 (filed with this Application). The equipment\nschedule below is a reference roster and does not restate the per-unit nameplate ratings recorded on\nthose datasheets.\n5.1 Inverters\nItem Manufacturer / Model Quantity Nameplate & Certification\nThe inverters will be configured at commissioning with fleet-wide export-limit settings to hold aggregate\nreal-power delivery at the point of common coupling to the Stated Capacity in Section 3.\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0231  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 3\n\n---\n\n5.2 PV Modules\nItem Manufacturer / Model Quantity STC Rating (per\nmodule)\n620 W bifacial mono-PERC modules\n(commercial-grade; subset of the ground-mount\ncount above; combined DC field)\n5.3 Balance-of-System\nAC combiner\nAC disconnect\nGrounding\nAnti-islanding / trip settings\nSection 6 — Construction and Commissioning Milestones (Applicant Estimate)\nMilestone schedule\nMilestones are applicant estimates and are subject to Alleniom study outcomes, equipment scheduling,\nand construction work-order execution.\nSection 7 — Processing Route and Applicant Notes\nProgram route requested Commercial DER Interconnection Application - reviewed at the Stated\nCapacity of 480 kW, export-limited operation\nRationale for route Stated Capacity below the 500 kW program-scope threshold via inverter\nexport-limit configuration; standard commercial rooftop/ground-mount\nconfiguration; behind-the-meter connection\nThe Applicant respectfully requests that this Application be screened at its Stated Capacity of 480 kW.\nWexley Distribution Center, at 8420 Corley Business Parkway, Halston, is undertaking a behind-the-meter\nground-mount and carport PV addition to offset a portion of its continuous warehouse and refrigeration\ndemand. The Developer of Record, Karsten Solar Development LLC, has been retained to design, permit,\nconstruct, and file for interconnection. The Applicant notes for the record: no existing DER is installed at\nthe service address, and no other DER filing has been made for this site.\nCorrespondence regarding this Application should be directed to Emery Traskin, Development Manager,\nKarsten Solar Development LLC, at the phone and email shown in Section 1, with copies to the Facilities\nManager at Wexley Distribution Center.\nSection 8 — Applicant Certification and Signature\nThe undersigned, as authorized Developer of Record for Wexley Distribution Center, certifies that:\n1.The information provided in this Application is true, accurate, and complete to the best of the\nDeveloper's and Applicant's knowledge as of the filing date.\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0231  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 4\n\n---\n\n2.The Applicant will comply with all applicable Alleniom Utilities interconnection standards, tariff\nprovisions, and the National Electrical Code as in effect at the time of interconnection.\n3.The Applicant will not energize the proposed DER in parallel with the utility system prior to receiving\nwritten Permission to Operate from Alleniom Utilities.\n4.The Applicant will notify Alleniom Utilities of any material change to the equipment, capacity, or point of\ninterconnection described in this Application.\n5.The inverter fleet identified in Section 5 will be configured at commissioning to hold aggregate\nreal-power delivery at the point of common coupling to the Stated Capacity of 480 kW — export-limited\noperation.\nApplicant\nSignatory Emery Traskin, Development Manager, Karsten Solar Development LLC -\nAuthorized Agent for Wexley Distribution Center\nSignature\nDate\nEmail\nFor DER Program Office Use Only\nApplication ID\nDate received\nIntake reviewer\nFeeder of record\nScreening status\nExisting-DER register check\nNotes Filed by Karsten Solar Development LLC on behalf of Wexley Distribution\nCenter. Filing declares Stated Capacity of 480 kW — export-limited operation.\nPer-unit inverter nameplate ratings are set out in the companion file Inverter\nNameplate & Spec Sheets — PXA-2025-0231, filed with this Application.\nForm footer — DER Program scope reference. Alleniom Utilities DER classes (per DIS-01 Rev 4 §3 and tariff §12.2):\nCommercial small-scale 500 kW–1 MW; medium-scale 1 MW–5 MW; program scope ≥500 kW; sub-500 kW DER\n(commercial and residential) is handled under the Simplified Small-Systems Process, outside the DER Program.\nDoc no. PXA-2025-0231 · Rev 0 · 06/09/2025 · Applicant: Wexley Distribution Center (Developer of Record: Karsten Solar\nDevelopment LLC)\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0231  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 5	<h1 id="pxa-2025-0231-stated-480kw">PXA-2025-0231 Stated 480kW</h1>\n<p>ALLENIOM UTILITIES — DER PROGRAM OFFICE<br>\nDER INTERCONNECTION APPLICATION (COMMERCIAL, ≥ 500<br>\nkW)<br>\nForm DIS-APP-01 · governed by DIS-01 Rev 4 · Alleniom DER Interconnection Standard<br>\nApplication ID: PXA-2025-0231<br>\nReceived (utility use only)<br>\nApplication version<br>\nFiling category<br>\nProcessing track requested<br>\nSection 1 — Applicant Information<br>\nApplicant / interconnection<br>\ncustomer<br>\nEntity type<br>\nCustomer mailing address<br>\nCustomer site contact<br>\nCustomer site phone<br>\nCustomer site email<br>\nDeveloper of record (preparer<br>\n&amp; filer)<br>\nDeveloper mailing address<br>