>\nreal-power delivery at the point of common coupling to the stated 480 kW value under all operating<br>\nconditions. On this basis the Applicant requests the Application be reviewed at the stated 480 kW figure.<br>\nSection 4 — Point of Interconnection<br>\nPoint of interconnection New 800 A, 3-phase back-fed breaker in the existing 480 V main distribution<br>\nswitchboard (MDS-1) in the warehouse main electrical room<br>\nDistance from PV combiner to<br>\nPOI<br>\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0231  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 2</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Point of common coupling<br>\nFeeder assignment<br>\nShared POI request (DIS-01<br>\n§3.5)<br>\n4.1 Connection Description<br>\nThe proposed PV system ties into the customer-owned side of the site's existing electrical service. Power<br>\nflow from the six commercial three-phase inverters (see the companion inverter datasheets file for per-unit<br>\nratings) is aggregated at PVC-1, routed through the pad-mount lockable AC disconnect (PVD-1), and<br>\nlands on a new 800 A back-fed breaker in MDS-1. MDS-1 is fed from the plant's existing utility service<br>\ntransformer through the site's existing 480 V main service disconnect and the existing utility revenue<br>\nmeter.<br>\nThe new PV interconnection is behind the existing service meter — the same point of common coupling<br>\nas the site's existing electrical service — on the load side of the utility revenue meter and upstream of the<br>\nwarehouse's process and refrigeration load buses.<br>\nNo new utility-side equipment, no new service transformer, no new service drop, and no separate revenue<br>\nmeter is requested. The Applicant proposes to net the PV generation against warehouse load through the<br>\nexisting bidirectional revenue meter of record and to hold export at the point of common coupling to the<br>\nStated Capacity of 480 kW under all operating conditions.<br>\nSection 5 — Equipment Schedule<br>\nThe proposed facility uses a fleet of commercial three-phase string inverters. Individual inverter nameplate<br>\nratings, model-level specifications, and manufacturer certifications are provided in the companion file<br>\nInverter Nameplate &amp; Spec Sheets — PXA-2025-0231 (filed with this Application). The equipment<br>\nschedule below is a reference roster and does not restate the per-unit nameplate ratings recorded on<br>\nthose datasheets.<br>\n5.1 Inverters<br>\nItem Manufacturer / Model Quantity Nameplate &amp; Certification<br>\nThe inverters will be configured at commissioning with fleet-wide export-limit settings to hold aggregate<br>\nreal-power delivery at the point of common coupling to the Stated Capacity in Section 3.<br>\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0231  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 3</p>\n<hr>\n<p>5.2 PV Modules<br>\nItem Manufacturer / Model Quantity STC Rating (per<br>\nmodule)<br>\n620 W bifacial mono-PERC modules<br>\n(commercial-grade; subset of the ground-mount<br>\ncount above; combined DC field)<br>\n5.3 Balance-of-System<br>\nAC combiner<br>\nAC disconnect<br>\nGrounding<br>\nAnti-islanding / trip settings<br>\nSection 6 — Construction and Commissioning Milestones (Applicant Estimate)<br>\nMilestone schedule<br>\nMilestones are applicant estimates and are subject to Alleniom study outcomes, equipment scheduling,<br>\nand construction work-order execution.<br>\nSection 7 — Processing Route and Applicant Notes<br>\nProgram route requested Commercial DER Interconnection Application - reviewed at the Stated<br>\nCapacity of 480 kW, export-limited operation<br>\nRationale for route Stated Capacity below the 500 kW program-scope threshold via inverter<br>\nexport-limit configuration; standard commercial rooftop/ground-mount<br>\nconfiguration; behind-the-meter connection<br>\nThe Applicant respectfully requests that this Application be screened at its Stated Capacity of 480 kW.<br>\nWexley Distribution Center, at 8420 Corley Business Parkway, Halston, is undertaking a behind-the-meter<br>\nground-mount and carport PV addition to offset a portion of its continuous warehouse and refrigeration<br>\ndemand. The Developer of Record, Karsten Solar Development LLC, has been retained to design, permit,<br>\nconstruct, and file for interconnection. The Applicant notes for the record: no existing DER is installed at<br>\nthe service address, and no other DER filing has been made for this site.<br>\nCorrespondence regarding this Application should be directed to Emery Traskin, Development Manager,<br>\nKarsten Solar Development LLC, at the phone and email shown in Section 1, with copies to the Facilities<br>\nManager at Wexley Distribution Center.<br>\nSection 8 — Applicant Certification and Signature<br>\nThe undersigned, as authorized Developer of Record for Wexley Distribution Center, certifies that:<br>\n1.The information provided in this Application is true, accurate, and complete to the best of the<br>\nDeveloper's and Applicant's knowledge as of the filing date.<br>\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0231  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 4</p>\n<hr>\n<p>2.The Applicant will comply with all applicable Alleniom Utilities interconnection standards, tariff<br>\nprovisions, and the National Electrical Code as in effect at the time of interconnection.<br>\n3.The Applicant will not energize the proposed DER in parallel with the utility system prior to receiving<br>\nwritten Permission to Operate from Alleniom Utilities.<br>\n4.The Applicant will notify Alleniom Utilities of any material change to the equipment, capacity, or point of<br>\ninterconnection described in this Application.<br>\n5.The inverter fleet identified in Section 5 will be configured at commissioning to hold aggregate<br>\nreal-power delivery at the point of common coupling to the Stated Capacity of 480 kW — export-limited<br>\noperation.<br>\nApplicant<br>\nSignatory Emery Traskin, Development Manager, Karsten Solar Development LLC -<br>\nAuthorized Agent for Wexley Distribution Center<br>\nSignature<br>\nDate<br>\nEmail<br>\nFor DER Program Office Use Only<br>\nApplication ID<br>\nDate received<br>\nIntake reviewer<br>\nFeeder of record<br>\nScreening status<br>\nExisting-DER register check<br>\nNotes Filed by Karsten Solar Development LLC on behalf of Wexley Distribution<br>\nCenter. Filing declares Stated Capacity of 480 kW — export-limited operation.<br>\nPer-unit inverter nameplate ratings are set out in the companion file Inverter<br>\nNameplate &amp; Spec Sheets — PXA-2025-0231, filed with this Application.<br>\nForm footer — DER Program scope reference. Alleniom Utilities DER classes (per DIS-01 Rev 4 §3 and tariff §12.2):<br>\nCommercial small-scale 500 kW–1 MW; medium-scale 1 MW–5 MW; program scope ≥500 kW; sub-500 kW DER<br>\n(commercial and residential) is handled under the Simplified Small-Systems Process, outside the DER Program.<br>\nDoc no. PXA-2025-0231 · Rev 0 · 06/09/2025 · Applicant: Wexley Distribution Center (Developer of Record: Karsten Solar<br>\nDevelopment LLC)<br>\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0231  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 5</p>	[]	markdown	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	markdown	en	31	31	{}
7	der-program/applications/pxa-2025-0244-merrow-creamery	102c97306aba561bc48e	PXA-2025-0244 Merrow Creamery	Application PXA-2025-0244 for a new 300 kW rooftop PV at the Merrow Creamery plant	f	t				# PXA-2025-0244 Merrow Creamery\n\nALLENIOM UTILITIES — DER PROGRAM OFFICE\nDER INTERCONNECTION APPLICATION (COMMERCIAL, ≥ 500\nkW)\nForm DIS-APP-01 · governed by DIS-01 Rev 4 · Alleniom DER Interconnection Standard\nApplication ID: PXA-2025-0244\nReceived (utility use only)\nApplication version\nFiling category\nProcessing track requested\nSection 1 — Applicant Information\nApplicant / interconnection\ncustomer\nEntity type\nMailing address\nPrimary contact\nContact phone\nContact email\nSigning authority\nPreparer\nThe Applicant certifies that it is the customer of record on the retail electric account serving the facility\nidentified in Section 2 and that all information provided in this Application is true and accurate to the best\nof its knowledge.\nSection 2 — Site Information\nFacility name\nService address\nFacility use\nRetail rate class\nExisting electric service\nExisting utility meter\nSite ownership\nFacility peak demand (last 12\nmonths, billed)\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0244  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 1\n\n---\n\nFacility minimum demand\n(24/7 process load)\nOperating schedule\nBackup generation on site\nSection 3 — Proposed DER\nDER technology\nProject description\nNameplate capacity (AC)\nDC module capacity\nMounting\nFuel / energy source\nOperating mode requested\nExport-limited operation?\nExpected export\nAnticipated in-service\n3.1 Preamble Note from Applicant\n"This new 300 kW rooftop PV system is separate from and unrelated to any existing equipment on site."\nSection 4 — Point of Interconnection\nPoint of interconnection New 400 A, 3-phase back-fed breaker in the existing 480 V main distribution\nswitchboard (MDS-1) located inside the Main Processing Building electrical\nroom\nDistance from PV combiner to\nPOI\nPoint of common coupling\nShared POI request (DIS-01\n§3.5)\n4.1 Connection Description\nThe proposed 300 kW PV system ties into the customer-owned side of the site's existing electrical service.\nPower flow from the three Solmery Power SM-100K-3P inverters is aggregated at the new PV AC\ncombiner (PVC-1), routed through a lockable utility-accessible AC disconnect (PVD-1), and lands on a\nnew 400 A back-fed breaker in the existing 480 V main distribution switchboard (MDS-1). MDS-1 is fed\nfrom the plant's existing utility service transformer through the site's existing 480 V main service\ndisconnect and the existing utility revenue meter.\nThe new PV interconnection is therefore behind the existing service meter — the same point of common\ncoupling as the site's existing electrical service — on the load side of the utility revenue meter and\nupstream of the plant's process load buses.\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0244  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 2\n\n---\n\nNo new utility-side equipment, no new service transformer, no new service drop, and no separate revenue\nmeter is requested. The Applicant proposes to net the PV generation against plant load through the\nexisting bidirectional revenue meter of record.\nSection 5 — Equipment Schedule\n5.1 Inverters\nItem Manufacturer / Model Qty AC Rating (per\nunit)\nTotal AC Certification\nSolmery Power SM-100K-3P\n(commercial three-phase string\ninverter)\n5.2 PV Modules\nItem Manufacturer / Model Qty STC Rating Total DC\n5.3 Balance of System\nAC combiner\nDC combiners\nPV disconnect\nGrounding\nAnti-islanding / trip settings\nSection 6 — Construction and Commissioning Milestones (Applicant Estimate)\nMilestone schedule\nMilestones are applicant estimates and are subject to Alleniom study outcomes, equipment scheduling,\nand construction work-order execution.\nSection 7 — Processing Route and Applicant Notes\nProgram route requested\nRationale for route Nameplate below 500 kW; low expected export given continuous process\nload; standard commercial rooftop configuration; UL 1741-SB certified\ninverters\nThe Applicant respectfully requests that this Application be screened under the applicable expedited\nprocess for commercial rooftop PV projects at or below 500 kW nameplate.\nThe Merrow Creamery facility at 5800 County Road F, Merrowfield is undertaking a rooftop PV addition to\noffset a portion of its continuous process electrical demand. The Applicant notes for the record: this new\n300 kW rooftop PV system is separate from and unrelated to any existing equipment on site. The\nApplicant is filing as a standalone project. No third-party developer, EPC, or aggregator is a party to this\nApplication.\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0244  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 3\n\n---\n\nCorrespondence regarding this Application should be directed to the Facilities & Utilities Manager at the\naddress, phone, and email shown in Section 1.\nSection 8 — Applicant Certification and Signature\nThe undersigned, on behalf of Merrow Creamery, certifies that:\n1.The information provided in this Application is true, accurate, and complete to the best of the\nApplicant's knowledge as of the filing date.\n2.The Applicant will comply with all applicable Alleniom Utilities interconnection standards, tariff\nprovisions, and the National Electrical Code as in effect at the time of interconnection.\n3.The Applicant will not energize the proposed DER in parallel with the utility system prior to receiving\nwritten Permission to Operate from Alleniom Utilities.\n4.The Applicant will notify Alleniom Utilities of any material change to the equipment, capacity, or point of\ninterconnection described in this Application.\nApplicant\nSignatory\nSignature\nDate\nEmail\nFor DER Program Office Use Only\nApplication ID\nDate received\nIntake reviewer\nScreening status\nExisting-DER register check\nNotes Filed as standalone commercial rooftop project at 300 kW nameplate.\nApplicant preamble states the new system is separate from and unrelated to\nany existing equipment on site. Connection description in Section 4 places\nnew PV interconnection behind the existing service meter at 5800 County\nRoad F.\nDoc no. PXA-2025-0244 · Rev 0 · 06/12/2025 · Applicant: Merrow Creamery\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0244  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 4	<h1 id="pxa-2025-0244-merrow-creamery">PXA-2025-0244 Merrow Creamery</h1>\n<p>ALLENIOM UTILITIES — DER PROGRAM OFFICE<br>\nDER INTERCONNECTION APPLICATION (COMMERCIAL, ≥ 500<br>\nkW)<br>\nForm DIS-APP-01 · governed by DIS-01 Rev 4 · Alleniom DER Interconnection Standard<br>\nApplication ID: PXA-2025-0244<br>\nReceived (utility use only)<br>\nApplication version<br>\nFiling category<br>\nProcessing track requested<br>\nSection 1 — Applicant Information<br>\nApplicant / interconnection<br>\ncustomer<br>\nEntity type<br>\nMailing address<br>\nPrimary contact<br>\nContact phone<br>\nContact email<br>\nSigning authority<br>\nPreparer<br>\nThe Applicant certifies that it is the customer of record on the retail electric account serving the facility<br>\nidentified in Section 2 and that all information provided in this Application is true and accurate to the best<br>\nof its knowledge.<br>\nSection 2 — Site Information<br>\nFacility name<br>\nService address<br>\nFacility use<br>\nRetail rate class<br>\nExisting electric service<br>\nExisting utility meter<br>\nSite ownership<br>\nFacility peak demand (last 12<br>\nmonths, billed)<br>\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0244  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 1</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Facility minimum demand<br>\n(24/7 process load)<br>\nOperating schedule<br>\nBackup generation on site<br>\nSection 3 — Proposed DER<br>\nDER technology<br>\nProject description<br>\nNameplate capacity (AC)<br>\nDC module capacity<br>\nMounting<br>\nFuel / energy source<br>\nOperating mode requested<br>\nExport-limited operation?<br>\nExpected export<br>\nAnticipated in-service<br>\n3.1 Preamble Note from Applic