DC<br>\n5.3 Balance of System<br>\nAC combiner<br>\nDC combiners<br>\nPV disconnect<br>\nGrounding<br>\nAnti-islanding / trip settings<br>\nSection 6 — Construction and Commissioning Milestones (Applicant Estimate)<br>\nMilestone schedule<br>\nMilestones are applicant estimates and are subject to Alleniom study outcomes, equipment scheduling,<br>\nand construction work-order execution.<br>\nSection 7 — Processing Route and Applicant Notes<br>\nProgram route requested<br>\nRationale for route Nameplate below 500 kW; low expected export given continuous process<br>\nload; standard commercial rooftop configuration; UL 1741-SB certified<br>\ninverters<br>\nThe Applicant respectfully requests that this Application be screened under the applicable expedited<br>\nprocess for commercial rooftop PV projects at or below 500 kW nameplate.<br>\nThe Merrow Creamery facility at 5800 County Road F, Merrowfield is undertaking a rooftop PV addition to<br>\noffset a portion of its continuous process electrical demand. The Applicant notes for the record: this new<br>\n300 kW rooftop PV system is separate from and unrelated to any existing equipment on site. The<br>\nApplicant is filing as a standalone project. No third-party developer, EPC, or aggregator is a party to this<br>\nApplication.<br>\nAlleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0244  |  DIS-APP-01  |  Page 3</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Correspondence regarding this Application should be directed to the Facilities &amp; Utilities Manager at the<br>\naddress, phone, and email shown in Section 1.<br>\nSection 8 — Applicant Certification and Signature<br>\nThe undersigned, on behalf of Merrow Creamery, certifies that:<br>\n1.The information provided in this Application is true, accurate, and complete to the best of the<br>\nApplicant's knowledge as of the filing date.<br>\n2.The Applicant will comply with all applicable Alleniom Utilities interconnection standards, tariff<br>\nprovisions, and the National Electrical Code as in effect at