23	der-program/equipment/2025-06-supplier-lead-time-report	265534019059226f9878	2025-06 Supplier Lead Time Report	June 2025 procurement status showing approximately 8-month supplier lead time for RTUs and POI reclosers	f	t				# 2025-06 Supplier Lead Time Report\n\n## Summary\n\n| Supplier Lead-Time Report — DER Program Equipment |   |\n| --- | --- |\n| Doc no. SCADA-EQP-2025-06  ·  Rev 1  ·  Date 06/30/2025  ·  Owner Marcus Deele |   |\n| Author: Marcus Deele, SCADA/EMS Engineering — marcus.deele@alleniom.com |   |\n| As of: 06/30/2025 |   |\n| Distribution: DER Program Office; Distribution Operations; Standards Engineering |   |\n| Field | Value |\n| Report | Supplier Lead-Time Report — DER Program Equipment (RTUs & POI reclosers) |\n| Prepared by | Marcus Deele, SCADA/EMS Engineering |\n| As of | 06/30/2025 |\n| Scope | Utility-owned RTU and POI recloser procurement in support of in-scope DER interconnection commissionings (≥500 kW). Program-owned only; customer-side equipment excluded. |\n| Current approved suppliers — RTU | Kelvraith Grid Systems, Inc. (approved supplier of record) |\n| Current approved suppliers — POI recloser | Norstead Power Controls, LLC (approved supplier of record) |\n| Quoted lead time — RTU | ~8-month lead time from PO acknowledgement to delivery to Halston staging yard |\n| Quoted lead time — POI recloser | ~8-month lead time from PO acknowledgement to delivery to Halston staging yard |\n| Lead-time framing | The ~8-month supplier lead time for RTUs and POI reclosers from the current approved suppliers, both device types, is a shortcoming of the current approved suppliers. Quoted intervals have not shortened materially through 2024–2025 despite repeated escalation with Kelvraith and Norstead account management. |\n| Incoming — 08/2025 | 2 RTU + POI recloser sets arriving 08/2025 (one complete set per site allocation). |\n| Incoming — 03/2026 | Next delivery 03/2026 (aggregated shipment covering remaining committed orders). |\n| Sites waiting on utility equipment | 7 completed sites awaiting utility equipment (construction complete; RTU and/or POI recloser outstanding). See companion tracker for site-level detail. |\n| Flag — grant-funded project | Grant-funded community project contracted in-service 09/30/2025 at risk. Alleron Community Solar Initiative — Rowan Hill (1.05 MW) requires RTU + POI recloser; only two sets land 08/2025 and the next window is 03/2026. |\n| Related standards | TCS-02 §5 (≥500 kW → utility RTU + SCADA telemetry); DPS-07 §4.2 / DIS-01 §5 (POI recloser applicability); OG-17 (deployment sequencing of constrained utility equipment). |\n| Companion files | DER-EQP-COMPL Completed_Sites_Awaiting_Equipment.xlsx (site-level roster); OG-17 Equipment Deployment Prioritization Guideline. |\n| Narrative notes |   |\n| • The ~8-month lead time is quoted by both current approved suppliers and has been reconfirmed by Kelvraith (RTU) on 06/12/2025 and by Norstead (POI recloser) on 06/18/2025 against outstanding purchase orders. |   |\n| • Neither supplier has offered an expedite fee schedule that would compress the interval below ~8 months. Requests for partial shipments have been declined by both suppliers on the basis of factory build slotting. |   |\n| • Vendor qualification of alternative sources for equivalent RTUs and POI reclosers is in progress; see Tab 3. |   |\n\n## Orders on Hand\n\n| Tab 2 — Orders on Hand |   |   |   |   |   |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Purchase orders currently in flight with the current approved suppliers. Quantities are program-owned sets (utility side of POI). "Set" = one RTU or one POI recloser unless noted. |   |   |   |   |   |\n| Supplier | Device | PO Number | PO Date | Qty | Expected Delivery |\n| Kelvraith Grid Systems, Inc. | RTU (utility-owned, SCADA-integrated per TCS-02 §5) | PO-ALN-2024-1187 | 12/09/2024 | 2 | 08/2025 |\n| Norstead Power Controls, LLC | POI recloser (utility-owned, distribution class) | PO-ALN-2024-1194 | 12/16/2024 | 2 | 08/2025 |\n| Kelvraith Grid Systems, Inc. / Norstead Power Controls, LLC (aggregated) | RTU + POI recloser sets (mixed shipment across both suppliers) | PO-ALN-2025-0403 / PO-ALN-2025-0417 | 07/22/2024 (Kelvraith) / 07/29/2024 (Norstead) — reissued 02/2025 for revised delivery slot | 5 RTU / 3 POI recloser | 03/2026 |\n| Notes |   |   |   |   |   |\n| • The 08/2025 shipments cover two complete site sets (one RTU + one POI recloser per site) and are the only utility equipment scheduled to land between the report date and the 09/30/2025 grant milestone. |   |   |   |   |   |\n| • The 03/2026 aggregated row reflects the next confirmed factory slot after 08/2025. Neither supplier has offered an intermediate delivery between these two dates. |   |   |   |   |   |\n| • All POs are firm-order, no-cancellation past factory-cut date. Kelvraith factory-cut for the 03/2026 batch occurred 03/2025; Norstead factory-cut occurred 04/2025. |   |   |   |   |   |\n\n## Open Vendor Queries\n\n| Tab 3 — Open Vendor Queries |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Alternative suppliers under evaluation for equivalent RTUs and POI reclosers, with the intent of qualifying a second source and shortening the ~8-month lead time from the current approved suppliers. Owner: Marcus Deele (SCADA/EMS Engineering). |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n| Query ID | Alternative Supplier | Device Category | Equivalent To | Status | Quoted Lead Time | Owner | Next Step |\n| VQ-2025-014 | Halbrent Substation Automation, GmbH | RTU | Kelvraith RTU platform | Datasheet + protocol compatibility review in progress | ~14 weeks quoted (unverified) | Marcus Deele | SCADA lab interoperability bench test 07/2025 |\n| VQ-2025-015 | Threydon Controls Corp. | RTU | Kelvraith RTU platform | Initial NDA executed 05/28/2025; awaiting reference-site list | Not yet quoted | Marcus Deele | Reference calls; UL / IEEE 1547 compliance letter |\n| VQ-2025-016 | Ferrowick Switchgear Ltd. | POI recloser | Norstead distribution-class recloser | Type-test documentation under review by Standards Engineering | ~18 weeks quoted (unverified) | Marcus Deele | Coordinate type-test acceptance with Evan Solberg |\n| VQ-2025-017 | Coastwide Electric Apparatus, Inc. | POI recloser | Norstead distribution-class recloser | Pre-qualification questionnaire returned 06/20/2025 | ~22 weeks quoted (unverified) | Marcus Deele | Factory audit scoping call scheduled 07/2025 |\n| VQ-2025-018 | Kelvraith Grid Systems, Inc. — engineering escalation | RTU | (incumbent) | Open request for expedited slot on outstanding PO-ALN-2025-0403 | No commitment offered | Marcus Deele | Quarterly account review 07/2025 |\n| VQ-2025-019 | Norstead Power Controls, LLC — engineering escalation | POI recloser | (incumbent) | Open request for expedited slot on outstanding PO-ALN-2025-0417 | No commitment offered | Marcus Deele | Quarterly account review 07/2025 |\n| Notes |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n| • None of the alternative suppliers listed have been added to the Alleniom approved-supplier list as of 06/30/2025. Any procurement action against VQ-2025-014 through VQ-2025-017 requires Standards Engineering type-test acceptance and Distribution Operations sign-off prior to PO issuance. |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n| • Lead-time quotes from alternative suppliers are preliminary and have not been validated against Alleniom-specific configuration (communications card, protection settings, mounting). |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n| • Second-source qualification will not affect the 08/2025 or 03/2026 deliveries already in flight from the current approved suppliers. |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n| End of report — Marcus Deele, SCADA/EMS Engineering, 06/30/2025. |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |	<h1 id="2025-06-supplier-lead-time-report">2025-06 Supplier Lead Time Report</h1>\n<h2 id="summary">Summary</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Supplier Lead-Time Report — DER Program Equipment</t