Next delivery 03/2026 (aggregated shipment covering remaining committed orders).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sites waiting on utility equipment</td>\n<td>7 completed sites awaiting utility equipment (construction complete; RTU and/or POI recloser outstanding). See companion tracker for site-level detail.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Flag — grant-funded project</td>\n<td>Grant-funded community project contracted in-service 09/30/2025 at risk. Alleron Community Solar Initiative — Rowan Hill (1.05 MW) requires RTU + POI recloser; only two sets land 08/2025 and the next window is 03/2026.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Related standards</td>\n<td>TCS-02 §5 (≥500 kW → utility RTU + SCADA telemetry); DPS-07 §4.2 / DIS-01 §5 (POI recloser applicability); OG-17 (deployment sequencing of constrained utility equipment).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Companion files</td>\n<td>DER-EQP-COMPL Completed_Sites_Awaiting_Equipment.xlsx (site-level roster); OG-17 Equipment Deployment Prioritization Guideline.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Narrative notes</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>• The ~8-month lead time is quoted by both current approved suppliers and has been reconfirmed by Kelvraith (RTU) on 06/12/2025 and by Norstead (POI recloser) on 06/18/2025 against outstanding purchase orders.</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>• Neither supplier has offered an expedite fee schedule that would compress the interval below ~8 months. Requests for partial shipments have been declined by both suppliers on the basis of factory build slotting.</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>• Vendor qualification of alternative sources for equivalent RTUs and POI reclosers is in progress; see Tab 3.</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id="orders-on-hand">Orders on Hand</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Tab 2 — Orders on Hand</th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Purchase orders currently in flight with the current approved suppliers. Quantities are program-owned sets 