s</th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Alternative suppliers under evaluation for equivalent RTUs and POI reclosers, with the intent of qualifying a second source and shortening the ~8-month lead time from the current approved suppliers. Owner: Marcus Deele (SCADA/EMS Engineering).</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Query ID</td>\n<td>Alternative Supplier</td>\n<td>Device Category</td>\n<td>Equivalent To</td>\n<td>Status</td>\n<td>Quoted Lead Time</td>\n<td>Owner</td>\n<td>Next Step</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>VQ-2025-014</td>\n<td>Halbrent Substation Automation, GmbH</td>\n<td>RTU</td>\n<td>Kelvraith RTU platform</td>\n<td>Datasheet + protocol compatibility review in progress</td>\n<td>~14 weeks quoted (unverified)</td>\n<td>Marcus Deele</td>\n<td>SCADA lab interoperability bench test 07/2025</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>VQ-2025-015</td>\n<td>Threydon Controls Corp.</td>\n<td>RTU</td>\n<td>Kelvraith RTU platform</td>\n<td>Initial NDA executed 05/28/2025; awaiting reference-site list</td>\n<td>Not yet quoted</td>\n<td>Marcus Deele</td>\n<td>Reference calls; UL / IEEE 1547 compliance letter</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>VQ-2025-016</td>\n<td>Ferrowick Switchgear Ltd.</td>\n<td>POI recloser</td>\n<td>Norstead distribution-class recloser</td>\n<td>Type-test documentation under review by Standards Engineering</td>\n<td>~18 weeks quoted (unverified)</td>\n<td>Marcus Deele</td>\n<td>Coordinate type-test acceptance with Evan Solberg</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>VQ-2025-017</td>\n<td>Coastwide Electric Apparatus, Inc.</td>\n<td>POI recloser</td>\n<td>Norstead distribution-class recloser</td>\n<td>Pre-qualification questionnaire returned 06/20/2025</td>\n<td>~22 weeks quoted (unverified)</td>\n<td>Marcus Deele</td>\n<td>Factory audit scoping call scheduled 07/2025</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>VQ-2025-018</td>\n<td>Kelvraith Grid Systems, Inc. — engineering escalation</td>\n<td>RTU</td>\n<td>(incumbent)</td>\n<td>Open request for expedited slot on outstanding PO-ALN-2025-0403</td>\n<td>No commitment offered</td>\n<td>Marcus Deele</td>\n<td>Quarterly account review 07/2025</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>VQ-2025-019</td>\n<td>Norstead Power Controls, LLC — engineering escalation</td>\n<td>POI recloser</td>\n<td>(incumbent)</td>\n<td>Open request for expedited slot on outstanding PO-ALN-2025-0417</td>\n<td>No commitment offered</td>\n<td>Marcus Deele</td>\n<td>Quarterly account review 07/2025</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Notes</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>• None of the alternative suppliers listed have been added to the Alleniom approved-supplier list as of 06/30/2025. Any procurement action against VQ-2025-014 through VQ-2025-017 requires Standards Engineering type-test acceptance and Distribution Operations sign-off prior to PO issuance.</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>• Lead-time quotes from alternative suppliers are preliminary and have not been validated against Alleniom-specific configuration (communications card, protection settings, mounting).</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>• Second-source qualification will not affect the 08/2025 or 03/2026 deliveries already in flight from the current approved suppliers.</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>End of report — Marcus Deele, SCADA/EMS Engineering, 06/30/2025.</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>	[]	markdown	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	markdown	en	10	10	{}
24	der-program/equipment/completed-sites-awaiting-equipment	b25f7ffc2fedbf2da8ff	Completed Sites Awaiting Equipment	Register of 7 completed sites awaiting utility equipment with raw attributes	f	t				# Completed Sites Awaiting Equipment\n\n## Register\n\n| Completed Sites Awaiting Utility Equipment |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Alleniom Utilities — DER Program Office · 4200 Veldmere Boulevard, Halston, Alleron 01HA · (612) 555-0100 · alleniom.com |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n| Doc no. DER-EQP-COMPL  ·  Rev 3  ·  Date 07/14/2025  ·  Owner DER Program Office |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n| Register | Completed Sites Awaiting Utility Equipment |   |   |   |   |   |\n| Maintained by | DER Program Office (der.program@alleniom.com) |   |   |   |   |   |\n| As of | 07/14/2025 |   |   |   |   |   |\n| Scope | In-scope DER interconnection sites (≥500 kW) that have reached construction complete and are awaiting utility-owned RTU and/or POI recloser to permit energization under TCS-02 §5. Standing register — no date prefix; refreshed weekly. |   |   |   |   |   |\n| Companion report | 2025-06_Supplier_Lead_Time_Report.xlsx (Marcus Deele, SCADA/EMS Engineering) |   |   |   |   |   |\n| Column note | "Requested Priority" reflects customer- or stakeholder-stated priority claims as received in writing; entries are transcribed verbatim from the requesting party's correspondence. |   |   |   |   |   |\n| Roster |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n| Site Name | Site Type | Contracted In-Service or Grant Deadline | Queue Date | Construction Complete Date | Required Devices | Requested Priority |\n| City of Elmsworth Northside Water Treatment Plant | municipal water treatment |   | 03/18/2024 | 05/02/2025 | RTU + POI recloser |   |\n| Alleron Community Solar Initiative — Rowan Hill (1.05 MW community solar) | grant-funded community solar | 09/30/2025 (grant funding) | 04/22/2024 | 06/06/2025 | RTU + POI recloser |   |\n| Brookfen North High School Array (720 kW) | school district (Brookfen USD) |   | 06/03/2024 | 04/18/2025 | RTU | HIGH — per school district |\n| Brookfen West Elementary Array (640 kW) | school district (Brookfen USD) |   | 07/08/2024 | 05/23/2025 | RTU | HIGH — per school district |\n| Vernand Logistics C&I Rooftop PV (620 kW) | commercial C&I |   | 05/14/2024 | 03/28/2025 | RTU |   |\n| Halstonfield Distribution Center PV (720 kW) | commercial C&I |   | 08/20/2024 | 06/13/2025 | RTU |   |\n| Prairie Corridor Business Park PV (860 kW) | commercial C&I |   | 09/12/2024 | 06/27/2025 | RTU + POI recloser |   |\n| Notes |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n| • | All seven sites are past construction complete and are held out of service pending utility-owned equipment installation and SCADA integration. TCS-02 §5 prohibits Permission to Operate absent live telemetry for sites ≥500 kW. |   |   |   |   |   |\n| • | Utility equipment supply status is tracked in the SCADA/EMS Supplier Lead-Time Report (Marcus Deele, 06/30/2025): two complete RTU + POI recloser sets are scheduled to arrive 08/2025; the next confirmed delivery is 03/2026. Current approved suppliers are Kelvraith Grid Systems, Inc. (RTU) and Norstead Power Controls, LLC (POI recloser), both quoting ~8-month lead times. |   |   |   |   |   |\n| • | "Requested Priority" entries against the two Brookfen USD school arrays were added to this register on 07/02/2025 following written escalation from Rosa Camarena, Facilities Director, Brookfen Unified School District. No other sites have priority claims on file as of this revision. |   |   |   |   |   |\n| • | The Alleron Community Solar Initiative — Rowan Hill row carries a contracted grant-funding in-service date of 09/30/2025, recorded in this register at application intake. |   |   |   |   |   |\n| • | Deployment sequencing of scarce utility equipment is governed by OG-17 (Equipment Deployment Prioritization Guideline, effective 04/07/2025). This register is an inputs roster; it does not itself assign sequencing. |   |   |   |   |   |\n| • | Register is maintained by the DER Program Office and refreshed on the weekly queue export cycle. Additions and removals are logged against the revision block above. |   |   |   |   |   |\n| Prepared by: DER Program Office, Alleniom Utilities — 07/14/2025. |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n\n## Column Definitions\n\n| Column Definitions |   |\n| --- | --- |\n| Register: Completed Sites Awaiting Utility Equipment  ·  Doc DER-EQP-COMPL Rev 3  ·  07/14/2025 |   |\n| Column | Definition |\n| Site Name | Site identifier as recorded in the DER Program queue. |\n| Site Type | Customer category (municipal essential service, grant-funded community solar, school district, commercial C&I). |\n| Contracted In-Service or Grant Deadline | Written contracted in-service date or grant-funding milestone, where one exists on file. Blank where no such deadline has been contracted or funded. |\n| Queue Date | Date the interconnection application received a queue position under the DER Program. |\n| Construction Complete Date | Date the site's customer-side construction was reported complete by the applicant and confirmed by field inspection. Not the same as PTO. |\n| Required Devices | Utility-owned equipment outstanding: RTU (per TCS-02 §5) and/or POI recloser (per DPS-07 §4.2 / per applicable Form ER-11 determination). |\n| Requested Priority | Priority level asserted by the customer or requesting stakeholder in written correspondence. Recorded as received; not a program determination. |	<h1 id="completed-sites-awaiting-equipment">Completed Sites Awaiting Equipment</h1>\n<h2 id="register">Register</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Completed Sites Awaiting Utility Equipment</th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Alleniom Utilities — DER Program Office · 4200 Veldmere Boulevard, Halston, Alleron 01HA · (612) 555-0100 · alleniom.com</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\