sted Priority" entries against the two Brookfen USD school arrays were added to this register on 07/02/2025 following written escalation from Rosa Camarena, Facilities Director, Brookfen Unified School District. No other sites have priority claims on file as of this revision.</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>•</td>\n<td>The Alleron Community Solar Initiative — Rowan Hill row carries a contracted grant-funding in-service date of 09/30/2025, recorded in this register at application intake.</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>•</td>\n<td>Deployment sequencing of scarce utility equipment is governed by OG-17 (Equipment Deployment Prioritization Guideline, effective 04/07/2025). This register is an inputs roster; it does not itself assign sequencing.</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>•</td>\n<td>Register is maintained by the DER Program Office and refreshed on the weekly queue export cycle. Additions and removals are logged against the revision block above.</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Prepared by: DER Program Office, Alleniom Utilities — 07/14/2025.</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id="column-definitions">Column Definitions</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Column Definitions</th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Register: Completed Sites Awaiting Utility Equipment  ·  Doc DER-EQP-COMPL Rev 3  ·  07/14/2025</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Column</td>\n<td>Definition</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Site Name</td>\n<td>Site identifier as recorded in the DER Program queue.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Site Type</td>\n<td>Customer category (municipal essential service, grant-funded community solar, school district, commercial C&amp;I).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Contracted In-Service or Grant Deadline</td>\n<td>Written contracted in-service date or grant-funding milestone, where one exists on file. Blank where no such deadline has been contracted or funded.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Queue Date</td>\n<td>Date the interconnection application received a queue position under the DER Program.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Construction Complete Date</td>\n<td>Date the site's customer-side construction was reported complete by the applicant and confirmed by field inspection. Not the same as PTO.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Required Devices</td>\n<td>Utility-owned equipment outstanding: RTU (per TCS-02 §5) and/or POI recloser (per DPS-07 §4.2 / per applicable Form ER-11 determination).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Requested Priority</td>\n<td>Priority level asserted by the customer or requesting stakeholder in written correspondence. Recorded as received; not a program determination.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>	[]	markdown	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	markdown	en	10	10	{}
25	der-program/equipment/soc-pto-hold-log	4cd0c3d4e3a63d3f9c97	SOC PTO Hold Log	SOC log of energization requests refused pending telemetry commissioning per TCS-02 section 5	f	t				# SOC PTO Hold Log\n\n## Register\n\n| SOC PTO-Hold Log |   |\n| --- | --- |\n| Alleniom Utilities — System Operations Center · 4200 Veldmere Boulevard, Halston, Alleron 01HA · (612) 555-0100 · alleniom.com |   |\n| Doc no. DER-EQP-SOC-PTOH · Rev — · Date 07/14/2025 · Owner SOC Shift Supervisor |   |\n| Register | SOC PTO-Hold Log — refusals of Permission to Operate on telemetry grounds |\n| Maintained by | Lena Kovalchuk, SOC Shift Supervisor (lena.kovalchuk@alleniom.com) |\n| As of | 07/14/2025 |\n| Standing note |   |\n| No PTO without live telemetry — TCS-02 §5 (no interim provision). All entries below are in-scope DER sites (≥500 kW) at which the utility-owned RTU is not physically installed, not commissioned end-to-end per TCS-02 §3.6, and not presenting valid points at the SCADA operator display. PTO is refused under TCS-02 §5 until the telemetry condition is satisfied. This log is refreshed on the SOC shift turnover cycle. |   |\n| SOC Notes |   |\n| 1. | All seven sites are construction-complete and are held out of service until utility-owned RTU install, end-to-end commissioning per TCS-02 §3.6, and valid points at SCADA per TCS-02 §6. |\n| 2. | TCS-02 §5 contains no interim provision. Absence of an interim clause is absence, not a stated exception. Requests for early, provisional, partial, or conditional operation are refused on the same basis and returned to the DER Program Office. |\n| 3. | Equipment supply and deployment sequencing are tracked by the DER Program Office (see companion register DER-EQP-COMPL, Completed Sites Awaiting Utility Equipment) and by SCADA/EMS Engineering (Marcus Deele). SOC does not sequence equipment; SOC confirms live telemetry at the moment PTO is requested. |\n| 4. | Requesting-party entries are transcribed from the written PTO request on file. Priority claims received from stakeholders are not tracked in this log; they are captured on DER-EQP-COMPL. |\n| 5. | Rows remain open until telemetry is confirmed live. Closure is logged against the interconnection file with SOC operator initials and timestamp. |\n| Prepared by: Lena Kovalchuk, SOC Shift Supervisor — 07/14/2025. |   |\n\n## Entries\n\n| SOC PTO-Hold Log — Entries |   |   |   |   |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Doc no. DER-EQP-SOC-PTOH · As of 07/14/2025 |   |   |   |   |\n| Site Name | Requesting Party | Request Date | Reason for Refusal | Standard Citation |\n| City of Elmsworth Northside Water Treatment Plant | Bill Tran, City of Elmsworth | 05/15/2025 | RTU/SCADA telemetry not installed | TCS-02 §5 |\n| Alleron Community Solar Initiative — Rowan Hill | Priya Halvorsen, Rowan Hill Community Solar LLC | 06/10/2025 | RTU/SCADA telemetry not installed | TCS-02 §5 |\n| Brookfen North High School Array | Rosa Camarena, Brookfen USD | 05/02/2025 | RTU/SCADA telemetry not installed | TCS-02 §5 |\n| Brookfen West Elementary Array | Rosa Camarena, Brookfen USD | 06/03/2025 | RTU/SCADA telemetry not installed | TCS-02 §5 |\n| Vernand Logistics C&I Rooftop PV | Derrick Muhlbach, Vernand Logistics, Inc. | 04/12/2025 | RTU/SCADA telemetry not installed | TCS-02 §5 |\n| Halstonfield Distribution Center PV | Owen Talbert-Reyes, Halstonfield Properties LLC | 06/20/2025 | RTU/SCADA telemetry not installed | TCS-02 §5 |\n| Prairie Corridor Business Park PV | Marisol Kettering, Prairie Corridor Development Partners | 07/01/2025 | RTU/SCADA telemetry not installed | TCS-02 §5 |	<h1 id="soc-pto-hold-log">SOC PTO Hold Log</h1>\n<h2 id="register">Register</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>SOC PTO-Hold Log</th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Alleniom Utilities — System Operations Center · 4200 Veldmere Boulevard, Halston, Alleron 01HA · (612) 555-0100 · alleniom.com</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Doc no. DER-EQP-SOC-PTOH · Rev — · Date 07/14/202