27	der-program/planning/2025-07-02-preapp-request-aln-108	0cd38c572c5fc61754e3	2025-07-02 PreApp Request ALN-108	Pre-application request for 3 MW project on Feeder ALN-108 quoting published 3.0 MW availability	f	t				# 2025-07-02 PreApp Request ALN-108\n\nNORTHLINE RENEWABLES LLC\nPRE-APPLICATION REQUEST\nFeeder Capacity Confirmation\nDate: July 2, 2025\nTo: Alleniom Utilities — DER Program Office\nder.program@alleniom.com\nFrom: Peter Ashford, Director of Project Development\nNorthline Renewables LLC\nSubject: Pre-Application Request — 3 MW project on Feeder ALN-108\nSUBMITTING PARTY\nDeveloper / Applicant\nBusiness address\nPrimary contact\nTelephone\nEmail\nREQUEST DETAILS\nField\nDate of submission\nAddressed to\nProgram inbox\nSubject\nRequested feeder\nSubstation area\nRequested project capacity\nDER category\nInterconnection type\nAnticipated technology\nSite status\nAnticipated in-service target\nSTATEMENT OF REQUEST\nNorthline Renewables LLC is pleased to submit this pre-application request to Alleniom Utilities for feeder\ncapacity confirmation in advance of formal application. We are developing a 3 MW pure-generation\n1840 Ferngate Parkway, Suite 210  ·  Halston, Alleron 02HA  ·  (612) 555-1826\n\n---\n\nphotovoltaic project sited within the Elderpine substation service area, and have identified Feeder ALN-108\nas the intended point of interconnection.\nIn preparation for this submittal, we have reviewed the Feeder Hosting Capacity Map published by\nAlleniom Utilities — Distribution Planning, which was the current published edition available at the time of\nour project sizing decisions.\nPer the published Hosting Capacity Map dated 05/15/2024, Feeder ALN-108 shows 3.0 MW of available\ncapacity. We wish to proceed with a 3 MW project at the Elderpine substation service area and request\nconfirmation.\nThe published map lists ALN-108 as a pure-generation feeder segment at 13.2 kV, with the last planning\nstudy reflected as 04/2024. Our proposed project is fully aligned with the DER category shown for the\nfeeder. Project capacity has been scoped at nameplate 3.0 MW so as to sit at, rather than above, the\npublished available figure — with the express intent of avoiding a request that would exceed the feeder's\nstated headroom.\nWe would appreciate written confirmation from the DER Program Office that the 3.0 MW published\navailability on Feeder ALN-108 remains current as of the date of this request, and guidance on the\npre-application dialogue steps Alleniom would like to conduct prior to our filing of a formal interconnection\napplication. Should Distribution Planning have updated feeder figures or study results that post-date the\n05/15/2024 publication, we would welcome the opportunity to receive that information so we can size the\nproject accordingly.\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\nProject name (working)\nElderpine Solar I\nNameplate DC\napproximately 3.9 MW-DC\nNameplate AC (interconnection\nrequest)\n3 MW-AC\nInverter topology\ncentral inverters with plant-level SCADA-compatible controller\nExport profile\n100% export; no on-site load\nEnvironmental / permitting\ninterconnection critical path; permitting proceeding in parallel\nREQUESTED RESPONSE\n1\nWritten confirmation of currently available capacity on Feeder ALN-108 for a pure-generation\ninterconnection at the requested 3 MW nameplate.\n2\nAny known conditions, restrictions, or upgrade indications identified by Distribution Planning that would\napply to a 3 MW project at this location.\n3\nScheduling of a pre-application dialogue meeting with Distribution Planning and the DER Program Office\nat Alleniom's earliest convenience.\nNorthline Renewables LLC appreciates the DER Program Office's consideration of this pre-application\nrequest. We remain available at the contact information above for any clarifying questions and stand ready\nto provide additional project detail as required.\nRespectfully submitted,\n\n\n---\n\n/s/ Peter Ashford\nPeter Ashford\nDirector of Project Development\nNorthline Renewables LLC\npeter.ashford@northlinerenewables.com  ·  (612) 555-1826\nDate signed: 07/02/2025\nEnclosure reference: Feeder Hosting Capacity Map, Alleniom Utilities — Distribution Planning, publication dated\n05/15/2024.	<h1 id="2025-07-02-preapp-request-aln-108">2025-07-02 PreApp Request ALN-108</h1>\n<p>NORTHLINE RENEWABLES LLC<br>\nPRE-APPLICATION REQUEST<br>\nFeeder Capacity Confirmation<br>\nDate: July 2, 2025<br>\nTo: Alleniom Utilities — DER Program Office<br>\nder.program@alleniom.com<br>\nFrom: Peter Ashford, Director of Project Development<br>\nNorthline Renewables LLC<br>\nSubject: Pre-Application Request — 3 MW project on Feeder ALN-108<br>\nSUBMITTING PARTY<br>\nDeveloper / Applicant<br>\nBusiness address<br>\nPrimary contact<br>\nTelephone<br>\nEmail<br>\nREQUEST DETAILS<br>\nField<br>\nDate of submission<br>\nAddressed to<br>\nProgram inbox<br>\nSubject<br>\nRequested feeder<br>\nSubstation area<br>\nRequested project capacity<br>\nDER category<br>\nInterconnection type<br>\nAnticipated technology<br>\nSite status<br>\nAnticipated in-service target<br>\nSTATEMENT OF REQUEST<br>\nNorthline Renewables LLC is pleased to submit this pre-application request to Alleniom Utilities for feeder<br>\ncapacity confirmation in advance of formal application. We are developing a 3 MW pure-generation<br>\n1840 Ferngate Parkway, Suite 210  ·  Halston, Alleron 02HA  ·  (612) 555-1826</p>\n<hr>\n<p>photovoltaic project sited within the Elderpine substation service area, and have identified Feeder ALN-108<br>\nas the intended point of interconnection.<br>\nIn preparation for this submittal, we have reviewed the Feeder Hosting Capacity Map published by<br>\nAlleniom Utilities — Distribution Planning, which was the current published edition available at the time of<br>\nour project sizing decisions.<br>\nPer the published Hosting Capacity Map dated 05/15/2024, Feeder ALN-108 shows 3.0 MW of available<br>\ncapacity. We wish to proceed with a 3 MW project at the Elderpine substation service area and request<br>\nconfirmation.<br>\nThe published map lists ALN-108 as a pure-generation feeder segment at 13.2 kV, with the last planning<br>\nstudy reflected as 04/2024. Our proposed project is fully aligned with the DER category shown for the<br>\nfeeder. Project capacity has been scoped at nameplate 3.0 MW so as to sit at, rather than above, the<br>\npublished available figure — with the express intent of avoiding a request that would exceed the feeder's<br>\nstated headroom.<br>\nWe would appreciate written confirmation from the DER Program Office that the 3.0 MW published<br>\navailability on Feeder ALN-108 remains current as of the date of this request, and guidance on the<br>\npre-application dialogue steps Alleniom would like to conduct prior to our filing of a formal interconnection<br>\napplication. Should Distribution Planning have updated feeder figures or study results that post-date the<br>\n05/15/2024 publication, we would welcome the opportunity to receive that information so we can size the<br>\nproject accordingly.<br>\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION<br>\nProject name (working)<br>\nElderpine Solar I<br>\nNameplate DC<br>\napproximately 3.9 MW-DC<br>\nNameplate AC (interconnection<br>\nrequest)<br>\n3 MW-AC<br>\nInverter topology<br>\ncentral inverters with plant-level SCADA-compatible controller<br>\nExport profile<br>\n100% export; no on-site load<br>\nEnvironmental / permitting<br>\ninterconnection critical path; permitting proceeding in parallel<br>\nREQUESTED RESPONSE<br>\n1<br>\nWritten confirmation of currently available capacity on Feeder ALN-108 for a pure-generation<br>\ninterconnection at the requested 3 MW nameplate.<br>\n2<br>\nAny known conditions, restrictions, or upgrade indications identified by Distribution Planning that would<br>\napply to a 3 MW project at this location.<br>\n3<br>\nScheduling of a pre-application dialogue meeting with Distribution Planning and the DER Program Office<br>\nat Alleniom's earliest convenience.<br>\nNorthline Renewables LLC appreciates the DER Program Office's consideration of this pre-application<br>\nrequest. We remain available at the contact information above for any clarifying questions and stand ready<br>\nto provide additional project detail as required.<br>\nRespectfully submitted,</p>\n<hr>\n<p>/s/ Peter Ashford<br>\nPeter Ashford<br>\nDirector of Project Development<br>\nNorthline Renewables LLC<br>\npeter.ashford@northlinerenewables.com  ·  (612) 555-1826<br>\nDate signed: 07/02/2025<br>\nEnclosure reference: Feeder Hosting Capacity Map, Alleniom Utilities — Distribution Planning, publication dated<br>\n05/15/2024.</p>	[]	markdown	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	markdown	en	35	35	{}
28	der-program/planning/hosting-capacity-map-export-2024-05-15	9d0f92c60174b5b7dd1f	Hosting Capacity Map Export 2024-05-15	Feeder-level hosting capacity export published 05/15/2024 with quarterly refresh commitment	f	t				# Hosting Capacity Map Export 2024-05-15\n\n## Title Block\n\n| Alleniom Utilities |   |\n| --- | --- |\n| Feeder Hosting Capacity Map Export |   |\n| Publication | Alleniom Utilities Feeder Hosting Capacity Map |\n| Published | 05/15/2024 |\n| Publishing organization | Alleniom Utilities — Distribution Planning |\n| Author | June Halloway, Distribution Planning Engineer |\n| Contact | june.halloway@alleniom.com |\n| Office | DER Program Office · 4200 Veldmere Boulevard, Halston, Alleron 01HA |\n| Refresh commitment | Quarterly refresh commitment. The map is republished on a quarterly cadence with updated published available capacity values incorporating incremental planning studies and material queue additions since the prior release. |\n| Refresh prioritization criteria | Refresh prioritization criteria: application date, capacity requested, DER category (net metering vs pure generation). Feeders with the earliest pending pre-application or application date receive priority for re-study, followed by feeders where the requested capacity is largest relative to the currently published available figure, followed by DER category weighting per the net metering vs pure generation distinction (pure-generation queue entries are weighted more heavily against feeder headroom than net-metering behind-the-meter entries at equivalent nameplate). |\n| Basis | Feeder-level planning study using recorded peak and minimum load, existing interconnected DER of record at the time of the underlying study, and standard thermal / voltage / protection screens per Alleniom Distribution Planning methodology. |\n| DER Category legend | "Net metering" — behind-the-meter DER netted against customer load at the point of common coupling. "Pure generation" — export-only front-of-the-meter DER. "Mixed" — feeder hosts a combination of net-metering and pure-generation interconnections. |\n| Voltage class note | Nominal voltages given as feeder primary line-to-line kV. |\n| Scope | Alleniom distribution system, all substations serving in-scope DER territory. Sub-transmission and transmission-connected resources excluded. |\n| Applicability | Values are the published available capacity figures as of the publication date shown above. Applicants and pre-application requesters should consult Distribution Planning for confirmation before finalizing project sizing decisions on any feeder shown. Published values do not reflect interconnection queue activity recorded after the publication date; the active-queue register maintained by the DER Program Office is the record of that activity. A pre-application capacity response is prepared against the published value as adjusted for queue entries added since publication. |\n| Document control | Doc no. HCM-2024-Q2 · Rev 1 · Date 05/15/2024 · Owner June Halloway |\n\n## Feeder Capacity\n\n| Feeder Capacity — Published Available (MW) |   |   |   |   |   |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Publication date: 05/15/2024 |   |   |   |   |   |\n| Feeder ID | Substation | Nominal Voltage | Published Available Capacity (MW) | DER Category | Last Study Date |\n| ALN-014 | Ashborne | 12.47 kV | 4.6 | Net Metering | 02/2024 |\n| ALN-023 | Ashborne | 12.47 kV | 2.1 | Mixed | 01/2024 |\n| ALN-031 | Brackenmoor | 13.2 kV | 5.9 | Pure Generation | 03/2024 |\n| ALN-042 | Brackenmoor | 13.2 kV | 2.7 | Pure Generation | 03/2024 |\n| ALN-055 | Cindermill | 12.47 kV | 3.4 | Net Metering | 11/2023 |\n| ALN-061 | Cindermill | 12.47 kV | 0.6 | Net Metering | 11/2023 |\n| ALN-074 | Downing Cross | 12.47 kV | 4.2 | Mixed | 02/2024 |\n| ALN-089 | Downing Cross | 12.47 kV | 2.9 | Net Metering | 02/2024 |\n| ALN-097 | Elderpine | 13.2 kV | 6.1 | Pure Generation | 04/2024 |\n| ALN-103 | Elderpine | 13.2 kV | 5.5 | Pure Generatio