pen Balance = Invoice Amount − Posted Amount as of the "As of" date above.</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>•  Rows without a Posted Date carry the full invoice amount as Open Balance and remain in the on-hold queue under non-payment status.</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>•  Domestic rooftop projects are outside DER program scope and are not tracked here.</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>	[]	markdown	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	markdown	en	12	12	{}
32	der-program/queue/notices/2025-04-22-noiw-pxa-2024-0161	0492015136d943d01fa6	2025-04-22 NOIW PXA-2024-0161	Formal Notice of Impending Withdrawal/Cancellation for PXA-2024-0161 sent 04/22/2025	f	t				# 2025-04-22 NOIW PXA-2024-0161\n\nALLENIOM UTILITIES\nDER Program Office  ·  Interconnection Studies\n(612) 555-0100  ·  alleniom.com\nNOTICE OF IMPENDING WITHDRAWAL / CANCELLATION\nIssued under APUC-filed Interconnection Tariff §12.4\nDate of Notice: 04/22/2025\nMethod of Delivery: Certified mail — return receipt requested\nUSPS Certified Article No.: 7015 1520 0002 4738 6194\nApplication Reference: PXA-2024-0161\nTo (Applicant of Record):\n1.  Reference to Pending Application\nThis notice concerns application PXA-2024-0161, on file with Alleniom Utilities' DER Interconnection\nProgram and currently held in the on-hold queue pending receipt of customer-provided information previously\nrequested by Interconnection Studies. The Company's outstanding request for information — most recently\nreiterated by written correspondence from Interconnection Studies to the applicant of record — has not received\na substantive response. Absent such a response, the application cannot be advanced through technical screening.\n2.  Tariff Basis\nPursuant to Alleniom's APUC-filed tariff §12.4, this Notice of Impending Withdrawal/Cancellation is hereby\nserved. If Alleniom Utilities does not receive a substantive response within 30 business days of the date of this\nnotice, the application shall be deemed withdrawn.\n3.  Business-Day Convention\nFor purposes of the response window established under §12.4, "business days" exclude Saturdays, Sundays, and\nfederal legal public holidays observed within the response period. Federal holidays falling within any portion of\nthe response window shall not be counted toward the 30-business-day period.\n4.  Response Deadline\nThe applicable response deadline shall be computed by adding thirty (30) business days to the date of this\nnotice, applying the business-day convention set out in §3 above. The applicant is responsible for computing the\napplicable deadline from the date shown at the top of this notice.\n5.  Required Response\nA substantive response consists of a written submission, addressed to Interconnection Studies at the address\nshown in the letterhead or by email to der.program@alleniom.com, that materially addresses the outstanding\ninformation request associated with PXA-2024-0161. The Company will treat the postmark date (for mailed\nsubmissions) or the timestamp of receipt (for electronic submissions) as the date of response.\nCorvale Public Library District\nAttn: Library Director\n410 Carrow Street\nCorvale, Alleron 18CV\n4200 Veldmere Boulevard, Halston, Alleron 01HA\n\n---\n\n6.  Consequence of Non-Response\nFailure to submit a substantive response within the period stated in §2 above shall result in application\nPXA-2024-0161 being deemed withdrawn and closed from the active queue without further action of the\nCompany, in accordance with §12.4. A subsequent DER interconnection request for the same site would require\nsubmission of a new application, which would take its own queue position as of the date determined complete.\n7.  Contact\nQuestions concerning the outstanding information request or the procedural effect of this notice may be directed\nto Interconnection Studies at der.program@alleniom.com or (612) 555-0100.\nSignature\nIssued by Interconnection Studies — Queue Administration, on behalf of:\n/s/ Meera Vellanki   (by queue administration)\nMeera Vellanki\nManager, Interconnection Studies\nAlleniom Utilities\nmeera.vellanki@alleniom.com\nCopy to file: PXA-2024-0161 / Notices\nCopy to: Withdrawal Notice Log (ICQ-WNL-STANDING)\nDocument Control\nDoc no. Rev Date Owner\nDelivery: certified mail, USPS Certified Article No. 7015 1520 0002 4738 6194  ·  Prepared 04/17/2025  ·  Released 04/22/2025  · \nRegister: Notices of Impending Withdrawal/Cancellation (Tariff §12.4)	<h1 id="2025-04-22-noiw-pxa-2024-0161">2025-04-22 NOIW PXA-2024-0161</h1>\n<p>ALLENIOM UTILITIES<br>\nDER Program Office  ·  Interconnection Studies<br>\n(612) 555-0100  ·  alleniom.com<br>\nNOTICE OF IMPENDING WITHDRAWAL / CANCELLATION<br>\nIssued under APUC-filed Interconnection Tariff §12.4<br>\nDate of Notice: 04/22/2025<br>\nMethod of Delivery: Certified mail — return receipt requested<br>\nUSPS Certified Article No.: 7015 1520 0002 4738 6194<br>\nApplication Reference: PXA-2024-0161<br>\nTo (Applicant of Record):<br>\n1.  Reference to Pending Application<br>\nThis notice concerns application PXA-2024-0161, on file with Alleniom Utilities' DER Interconnection<br>\nProgram and currently held in the on-hold queue pending receipt of customer-provided information previously<br>\nrequested by Interconnection Studies. The Company's outstanding request for information — most recently<br>\nreiterated by written correspondence from Interconnection Studies to the applicant of record — has not received<br>\na substantive response. Absent such a response, the application cannot be advanced through technical screening.<br>\n2.  Tariff Basis<br>\nPursuant to Alleniom's APUC-filed tariff §12.4, this Notice of Impending Withdrawal/Cancellation is hereby<br>\nserved. If Alleniom Utilities does not receive a substantive response within 30 business days of the date of this<br>\nnotice, the application shall be deemed withdrawn.<br>\n3.  Business-Day Convention<br>\nFor purposes of the response window established under §12.4, "business days" exclude Saturdays, Sundays, and<br>\nfederal legal public holidays observed within the response period. Federal holidays falling within any portion of<br>\nthe response window shall not be counted toward the 30-business-day period.<br>\n4.  Response Deadline<br>\nThe applicable response deadline shall be computed by adding thirty (30) business days to the date of this<br>\nnotice, applying the business-day convention set out in §3 above. The applicant is responsible for computing the<br>\napplicable deadline from the date shown at the top of this notice.<br>\n5.  Required Response<br>\nA substantive response consists of a written submission, addressed to Interconnection Studies at the address<br>\nshown in the letterhead or by email to der.program@alleniom.com, that materially addresses the outstanding<br>\ninformation request associated with PXA-2024-0161. The Company will treat the postmark date (for mailed<br>\nsubmissions) or the timestamp of receipt (for electronic submissions) as the date of response.<br>\nCorvale Public Library District<br>\nAttn: Library Director<br>\n410 Carrow Street<br>\nCorvale, Alleron 18CV<br>\n4200 Veldmere Boulevard, Halston, Alleron 01HA</p>\n<hr>\n<ol>\n<li>Consequence of Non-Response<br>\nFailure to submit a substantive response within the period stated in §2 above shall result in application<br>\nPXA-2024-0161 being deemed withdrawn and closed from the active queue without further action of the<br>\nCompany, in accordance with §12.4. A subsequent DER interconnection request for the same site would require<br>\nsubmission of a new application, which would take its own queue position as of the date determined complete.</li>\n<li>Contact<br>\nQuestions concerning the outstanding information request or the procedural effect of this notice may be directed<br>\nto Interconnection Studies at der.program@alleniom.com or (612) 555-0100.<br>\nSignature<br>\nIssued by Interconnection Studies — Queue Administration, on behalf of:<br>\n/s/ Meera Vellanki   (by queue administration)<br>\nMeera Vellanki<br>\nManager, Interconnection Studies<br>\nAlleniom Utilities<br>\nmeera.vellanki@alleniom.com<br>\nCopy to file: PXA-2024-0161 / Notices<br>\nCopy to: Withdrawal Notice Log (ICQ-WNL-STANDING)<br>\nDocument Control<br>\nDoc no. Rev Date Owner<br>\nDelivery: certified mail, USPS Certified Article No. 7015 1520 0002 4738 6194  ·  Prepared 04/17/2025  ·  Released 04/22/2025  · <br>\nRegister: Notices of Impending Withdrawal/Cancellation (Tariff §12.4)</li>\n</ol>	[]	markdown	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	markdown	en	5	5	{}
