fore the effective date of the Telemetry &amp; Communications Standard (TCS-02, effective 06/01/2021) and was accepted under the telemetry provisions in force at commissioning. This annotation does not confer a permanent exemption: per TCS-02 §2(d), a pre-TCS-02 site is brought into TCS-02 scope when it is the subject of a new interconnection application. Status values in this column are informational; this register does not independently determine upgrade eligibility or compliance.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3.</td>\n<td>Sites listed as decommissioned or inactive are retained in the register for address-history purposes and are excluded from active-DER counts.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4.</td>\n<td>Address matches are performed on normalized premise address. Multiple DER at a single service address are listed as separate rows.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5.</td>\n<td>Extract does not include applications currently in queue (see Active Queue Report).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6.</td>\n<td>Current Status color key: green = operational with TCS-02-compliant telemetry (utility RTU); amber = in service under a pre-TCS-02 telemetry arrangement (no telemetry or legacy analog/dial-up/modem/SCADA); red = decommissioned or inactive.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>	[]	markdown	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	2026-11-20T11:40:53.219780+00:00	markdown	en	5	5	{}
