40	der-program/standards/cel-2025-q2-certified-equipment-list	70d94e9494953ffa2bf1	CEL-2025-Q2 Certified Equipment List	Current Certified Equipment List published 04/30/2025 superseding CEL-2024-Q4	f	t				# CEL-2025-Q2 Certified Equipment List\n\n## Front Matter\n\n| Alleniom Utilities — Certified Equipment List |   |\n| --- | --- |\n| Edition: CEL-2025-Q2 · Published 04/30/2025 · Supersedes CEL-2024-Q4 (published 10/31/2024). |   |\n| PCS listing basis: UL 1741-SB / UL 3141. |   |\n| Doc no. | CEL-2025-Q2 |\n| Revision | Q2-2025 |\n| Effective date | 04/30/2025 |\n| Supersedes | CEL-2024-Q4 (10/31/2024) |\n| Owner | Standards Engineering (Evan Solberg) |\n| Approved by | Manager, Standards Engineering |\n| Distribution | DER Program Office; Interconnection Studies; DER Planning Group; SCADA/EMS Engineering; Commissioning; Regulatory Affairs; contracted developers on request |\n| Next scheduled edition | CEL-2025-Q3 (planned 07/31/2025) |\n| Cross-reference — DIS-01 Rev 4 §3.6 (Controlled-capacity recognition) |   |\n| A limit below nameplate is recognized only with a valid UL 1741 / UL 3141 PCS certification plus an approved Control Narrative — sufficient in themselves for recognition. Where the site's arrangement includes utility equipment, the recognized limit is enforced as applicable: telemetry monitoring, and on pure-generation sites the POI recloser's ANSI 32 directional-power element set to the recognized limit and tripping on violation. |   |\n| How to use this list |   |\n| The Inverters tab lists smart-inverter models with a valid UL 1741-SB certification of record as of the edition date. The Power Control Systems tab lists UL 3141-certified PCS assemblies eligible to satisfy the controlled-capacity recognition path under DIS-01 §3.6. Listing on this edition does not by itself authorize interconnection; project-specific screening, protection, and commissioning requirements continue to apply. Models superseded, delisted, or withdrawn between quarterly editions are removed from the current tab; superseded editions remain available through Standards Engineering on request. |   |\n| Change summary since CEL-2024-Q4 |   |\n| — 8 inverter models added on new UL 1741-SB certifications received 11/2024–04/2025. |   |\n| — 2 inverter models removed — manufacturer discontinued line or certification not renewed under UL 1741-SB. |   |\n| — 3 PCS models added (Quenda Controls QC-PCS-250; Verronex Power Systems VPS-Cap-1500; Verronex Power Systems VPS-Cap-3000). |   |\n| — All Torvane Electric TE-75K rows recertified to UL 1741-SB; superseded UL 1741 (non-SB) entry retired. |   |\n| Contact | Evan Solberg, Standards Engineering — evan.solberg@alleniom.com · (612) 555-0113 |\n\n## Inverters\n\n| Manufacturer | Model | Rated kW | Listing Basis | Effective Date | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Solmery Power | SM-60K-3P | 60 | UL 1741-SB | 03/14/2024 | Three-phase string inverter; carried from CEL-2024-Q4. |\n| Solmery Power | SM-100K-3P | 100 | UL 1741-SB | 03/14/2024 | Three-phase string inverter. |\n| Solmery Power | SM-125K-3P | 125 | UL 1741-SB | 03/14/2024 | Carried from CEL-2024-Q4. |\n| Solmery Power | SM-160K-3P | 160 | UL 1741-SB | 07/22/2024 | — |\n| Solmery Power | SM-215K-3P | 215 | UL 1741-SB | 11/18/2024 | Carried from CEL-2024-Q4 (Q4 addendum listing). |\n| Solmery Power | SM-245K-3P | 245 | UL 1741-SB | 01/27/2025 | Carried from CEL-2024-Q4 (Q4 addendum listing). |\n| Solmery Power | SM-300K-3P | 300 | UL 1741-SB | 03/03/2025 | Three-phase central-string. |\n| Torvane Electric | TE-33K | 33 | UL 1741-SB | 11/05/2024 | — |\n| Torvane Electric | TE-75K | 75 | UL 1741-SB | 02/12/2025 | Recertified to SB profile; prior UL 1741 record retired. |\n| Torvane Electric | TE-100K | 100 | UL 1741-SB | 11/05/2024 | — |\n| Torvane Electric | TE-125K | 125 | UL 1741-SB | 11/05/2024 | — |\n| Torvane Electric | TE-150K | 150 | UL 1741-SB | 12/09/2024 | New listing this edition. |\n| Torvane Electric | TE-180K | 180 | UL 1741-SB | 12/09/2024 | Carried from CEL-2024-Q4 (Q4 addendum listing). |\n| Torvane Electric | TE-225K | 225 | UL 1741-SB | 02/28/2025 | — |\n| Vexlar Energy | VX-50C | 50 | UL 1741-SB | 06/02/2024 | — |\n| Vexlar Energy | VX-90C | 90 | UL 1741-SB | 06/02/2024 | — |\n| Vexlar Energy | VX-140C | 140 | UL 1741-SB | 09/16/2024 | Carried from prior edition. |\n| Vexlar Energy | VX-200C | 200 | UL 1741-SB | 06/02/2024 | — |\n| Vexlar Energy | VX-250C | 250 | UL 1741-SB | 06/02/2024 | Carried from CEL-2024-Q4. |\n| Vexlar Energy | VX-320C | 320 | UL 1741-SB | 02/04/2025 | New listing this edition. |\n| Halbrick Solar | HB-50 | 50 | UL 1741-SB | 04/19/2024 | Single-phase 208 V. |\n| Halbrick Solar | HB-125 | 125 | UL 1741-SB | 04/19/2024 | — |\n| Halbrick Solar | HB-250 | 250 | UL 1741-SB | 08/07/2024 | — |\n| Fenwyck Power | FW-Grid 100 | 100 | UL 1741-SB | 05/23/2024 | — |\n| Fenwyck Power | FW-Grid 175 | 175 | UL 1741-SB | 10/14/2024 | — |\n| Fenwyck Power | FW-Grid 275 | 275 | UL 1741-SB | 01/13/2025 | New listing this edition. |\n| Ostreme Electric | OE-3P-60 | 60 | UL 1741-SB | 05/06/2024 | — |\n| Ostreme Electric | OE-3P-150 | 150 | UL 1741-SB | 05/06/2024 | — |\n| Ostreme Electric | OE-3P-330 | 330 | UL 1741-SB | 02/17/2025 | New listing this edition. |\n| Nordreem Grid | NG-XT-125 | 125 | UL 1741-SB | 08/26/2024 | — |\n| Nordreem Grid | NG-XT-225 | 225 | UL 1741-SB | 12/16/2024 | New listing this edition. |\n| Cerlant PV | CL-208-100 | 100 | UL 1741-SB | 07/08/2024 | Low-voltage commercial. |\n| Cerlant PV | CL-480-250 | 250 | UL 1741-SB | 07/08/2024 | 480 V commercial three-phase. |\n| Marlweth Inverter | MW-Central 500 | 500 | UL 1741-SB | 03/10/2025 | New listing this edition; central inverter, ≥500 kW class. |\n\n## Power Control Systems\n\n| Manufacturer | Model | Rated kW | Listing Basis | Effective Date | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Quenda Controls | QC-PCS-250 | 250 | UL 3141 | 02/24/2025 | New listing this edition; suitable for small commercial export-limiting. |\n| Quenda Controls | QC-PCS-500 | 500 | UL 3141 | 09/27/2024 | Carried from CEL-2024-Q4. |\n| Quenda Controls | QC-PCS-1000 | 1000 | UL 3141 | 09/27/2024 | Carried from CEL-2024-Q4. |\n| Delrix Grid Sciences | DGS-PCS-2000 | 2000 | UL 3141 | 12/04/2024 | Medium-scale central PCS. |\n| Verronex Power Systems | VPS-Cap-1500 | 1500 | UL 3141 | 03/28/2025 | New listing this edition. |\n| Verronex Power Systems | VPS-Cap-3000 | 3000 | UL 3141 | 03/28/2025 | New listing this edition; medium-scale (1–5 MW) applications. |\n\n## Notes and Cross-References\n\n| Item | Reference |\n| --- | --- |\n| Controlled-capacity recognition | DIS-01 Rev 4 §3.6 — restated verbatim in Front Matter. |\n| Telemetry & communications for ≥500 kW | TCS-02 §5. |\n| Protective device requirements at export-capable POI | DPS-07 Rev 2 §4.2. |\n| Standards conflict routing | ERP-9 §3 (Form ER-11); Bulletin EB-2025-03 (03/24/2025). |\n| Witness test & waiver eligibility | Witness Test & Waiver Procedure (Standards Engineering) — eligibility requires the installed inverter to appear on the CURRENT CEL edition. |\n| Superseded editions | CEL-2024-Q4 (published 10/31/2024) is superseded by this edition and is not to be used for new commissioning determinations. |\n| Listing removals | Models delisted between editions are removed from the current tabs without further notation; historical certification records are retained by Standards Engineering. |	<h1 id="cel-2025-q2-certified-equipment-list">CEL-2025-Q2 Certified Equipment List</h1>\n<h2 id="front-matter">Front Matter</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Alleniom Utilities — Certified Equipment List</th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Edition: CEL-2025-Q2 · Published 04/30/2025 · Supersedes CEL-2024-Q4 (published 10/31/2024).</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PCS listing basis: UL 1741-SB / UL 3141.</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Doc no.</td>\n<td>CEL-2025-Q2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Revision</td>\n<td>Q2-2025</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Effective date</td>\n<td>04/30/2025</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supersedes</td>\n<td>CEL-2024-Q4 (10/31/2024)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Owner</td>\n<td>Standards Engineering (Evan Solberg)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Approved by</td>\n<td>Manager, Standards Engineering</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Distribution</td>\n<td>DER Program Office; Interconnection Studies; DER Planning Group; SCADA/EMS Engineering; Commissioning; Regulatory Affairs; contracted developers on request</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Next scheduled edition</td>\n<td>CEL-2025-Q3 (planned 07/31/2025)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cross-reference — DIS-01 Rev 4 §3.6 (Controlled-capacity recognition)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A limit below nameplate is recognized only with a valid UL 1741 / UL 3141 PCS certification plus an approved Control Narrative — sufficient in themselves for recognition. Where the site's arrangement includes utility equipment, the recognized limit is enforced as applicable: telemetry monitoring, and on pure-generation sites the POI recloser's ANSI 32 directional-power element set to the recognized limit and tripping on violation.</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>How to use this list</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>The Inverters tab lists smart-inverter models with a valid UL 1741-SB certification of record as of the edition date. The Power Control Systems tab lists UL 3141-certified PCS assemblies eligible to satisfy the controlled-capacity recognition path under DIS-01 §3.6. Listing on this edition does not by itself authorize interconnection; project-specific screening, protection, and commissioning requirements continue to apply. Models superseded, delisted, or withdrawn between quarterly editions are removed from the current tab; superseded editions remain available through Standards Engineering on request.</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Change summary since CEL-2024-Q4</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>— 8 inverter models added on new UL 1741-SB certifications received 11/2024–04/2025.</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>— 2 inverter models removed — manufacturer discontinued line or certification not renewed under UL 1741-SB.</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>— 3 PCS models added (Quenda Controls QC-PCS-250; Verronex Power Systems VPS-Cap-1500; Verronex Power Systems VPS-Cap-3000).</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>— All Torvane Electric TE-75K rows recertified to UL 1741-SB; superseded UL 1741 (non-SB) entry retired.</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Contact</td>\n<td>Evan Solberg, Standards Engineering — evan.solberg@alleniom.com · (612) 555-0113</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id="inverters">Inverters</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Manufacturer</th>\n<th>Model</th>\n<th>Rated kW</th>\n<th>Listing Basis</th>\n<th>Effective Date</th>\n<th>Notes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Solmery Power</td>\n<td>SM-60K-3P</td>\n<td>60</td>\n<td>UL 1741-SB</td>\n<td>03/14/2024</td>\n<td>Three-phase string inverter; carried from CEL-2024-Q4.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Solmery Power</td>\n<td>SM-100K-3P</td>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>UL 1741-SB</td>\n<td>03/14/2024</td>\n<td>Three-phase string inverter.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Solmery Power</td>\n<td>SM-125K-3P</td>\n<td>125</td>\n<td>UL 1741-SB</td>\n<td>03/14/2024</td>\n<td>Carried from CEL-2024-Q4.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Solmery Power</td>\n<td>SM-160K-3P</td>\n<td>160</td>\n<td>UL 1741-SB</td>\n<td>07/22/2024</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Solmery Power</td>\n<td>SM-215K-3P</td>\n<td>215</td>\n<td>UL 1741-SB</td>\n<td>11/18/2024</td>\n<td>Carried from CEL-2024-Q4 (Q4 addendum listing).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Solmery Power</td>\n<td>SM-245K-3P</td>\n<td>245</td>\n<td>UL 1741-SB</td>\n<td>01/27/2025</td>\n<td>Carried from CEL-2024-Q4 (Q4 addendum listing).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Solmery Power</td>\n<td>SM-300K-3P</td>\n<td>300</td>\n<td>UL 1741-SB</td>\n<td>03/03/2025</td>\n<td>Three-phase central-string.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Torvane Electric</td>\n<td>TE-33K</td>\n<td