52	der-program/studies/bramwick-commons-screening-memo-v1	bf726e0f17ec6ff7e606	Bramwick Commons Screening Memo v1	Screening memo for Bramwick Commons Solar on Feeder ALN-214 using overnight minimum load	f	t				# Bramwick Commons Screening Memo v1\n\nAlleniom Utilities — DER Program Office\n4200 Veldmere Boulevard, Halston, Alleron 01HA  ·  (612) 555-0100  ·  alleniom.com\nSUPPLEMENTAL REVIEW SCREEN DETERMINATION\nTo:      Meera Vellanki, Manager, Interconnection Studies\nFrom:   Priya Ranganathan, Interconnection Studies\nDate:   06/25/2025\nSubject: Bramwick Commons Solar (1.8 MW, Feeder ALN-214) — Supplemental Review Screen Determination\n1. Project\nThe application was routed to supplemental review following failure of an initial fast-track screen. This memo records the disposition of the 100%-of-minimum-load screen applied under SRP-3 Rev 3.\n2. Screen applied\n100%-of-minimum-load screen for solar, per §4 of SRP-3 (Rev 3, effective 02/10/2025). Under this screen, the requested DER capacity is compared against the minimum load observed on the subject feeder from AMI interval data.\n3. Analysis\nReviewed AMI interval load data for Feeder ALN-214 from the Alleniom AMI Data Warehouse and identified a minimum feeder load of 1.1 MW. The value was drawn from the feeder AMI record available on file for ALN-214. No intervals were excluded for known feeder outages, load transfers, or planned switching during the period reviewed.\n4. Comparison\n1.8 MW requested exceeds 1.1 MW minimum feeder load — screen FAILED.\n5. Recommendation\nStudy Agreement required prior to advancement. The application should not proceed on the supplemental-review track. A Study Agreement should be offered to Bramwick Commons Solar LLC, with the scope covering the technical conditions that gave rise to the failed screen on Feeder ALN-214.\n6. Disposition\nReturn supplemental review file to Interconnection Studies queue with a failed-screen flag on Feeder ALN-214.\nNotify the applicant of the screen result and forward the Study Agreement package.\nHold advancement of PXA record for Bramwick Commons Solar until Study Agreement is executed.\nSigned:\nPriya Ranganathan\nStaff Analyst, Interconnection Studies\nAlleniom Utilities\npriya.ranganathan@alleniom.com\n06/25/2025\nReviewed by:\n/s/ Meera Vellanki\nMeera Vellanki\nManager, Interconnection Studies\n06/25/2025\nFile: /DER_Program/Studies/Bramwick_Commons_Screening_Memo_v1.docx\nReference standard: SRP-3 Rev 3 §4 (Supplemental Review Procedure)\n\n| Doc no. | Rev | Date | Owner |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| IS-BRAM-2025-06-25 | v1 | 06/25/2025 | Interconnection Studies |\n\n\n| Item | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Applicant | Bramwick Commons Solar LLC |\n| Project | Bramwick Commons Solar |\n| Requested capacity | 1.8 MW |\n| Point of interconnection | Feeder ALN-214 |\n| Resource type | Solar photovoltaic |\n\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Subject feeder | ALN-214 |\n| Data source | Alleniom AMI Data Warehouse — feeder-aggregate interval data |\n| Data window | 06/24/2024 – 06/24/2025 (12 months of AMI data available on file) |\n| Interval cadence | Sixty (60) minutes |\n| Feeder minimum load identified | 1.1 MW |\n\n\n| Requested capacity | Feeder minimum load | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1.8 MW | 1.1 MW | FAILED |	<h1 id="bramwick-commons-screening-memo-v1">Bramwick Commons Screening Memo v1</h1>\n<p>Alleniom Utilities — DER Program Office<br>\n4200 Veldmere Boulevard, Halston, Alleron 01HA  ·  (612) 555-0100  ·  alleniom.com<br>\nSUPPLEMENTAL REVIEW SCREEN DETERMINATION<br>\nTo:      Meera Vellanki, Manager, Interconnection Studies<br>\nFrom:   Priya Ranganathan, Interconnection Studies<br>\nDate:   06/25/2025<br>\nSubject: Bramwick Commons Solar (1.8 MW, Feeder ALN-214) — Supplemental Review Screen Determination<br>\n1. Project<br>\nThe application was routed to supplemental review following failure of an initial fast-track screen. This memo records the disposition of the 100%-of-minimum-load screen applied under SRP-3 Rev 3.<br>\n2. Screen applied<br>\n100%-of-minimum-load screen for solar, per §4 of SRP-3 (Rev 3, effective 02/10/2025). Under this screen, the requested DER capacity is compared against the minimum load observed on the subject feeder from AMI interval data.<br>\n3. Analysis<br>\nReviewed AMI interval load data for Feeder ALN-214 from the Alleniom AMI Data Warehouse and identified a minimum feeder load of 1.1 MW. The value was drawn from the feeder AMI record available on file for ALN-214. No intervals were excluded for known feeder outages, load transfers, or planned switching during the period reviewed.<br>\n4. Comparison<br>\n1.8 MW requested exceeds 1.1 MW minimum feeder load — screen FAILED.<br>\n5. Recommendation<br>\nStudy Agreement required prior to advancement. The application should not proceed on the supplemental-review track. A Study Agreement should be offered to Bramwick Commons Solar LLC, with the scope covering the technical conditions that gave rise to the failed screen on Feeder ALN-214.<br>\n6. Disposition<br>\nReturn supplemental review file to Interconnection Studies queue with a failed-screen flag on Feeder ALN-214.<br>\nNotify the applicant of the screen result and forward the Study Agreement package.<br>\nHold advancement of PXA record for Bramwick Commons Solar until Study Agreement is executed.<br>\nSigned:<br>\nPriya Ranganathan<br>\nStaff Analyst, Interconnection Studies<br>\nAlleniom Utilities<br>\npriya.ranganathan@alleniom.com<br>\n06/25/2025<br>\nReviewed by:<br>\n/s/ Meera Vellanki<br>\nMeera Vellanki<br>\nManager, Interconnection Studies<br>\n06/25/2025<br>\nFile: /DER_Program/Studies/Bramwick_Commons_Screening_Memo_v1.docx<br>\nReference standard: SRP-3 Rev 3 §4 (Supplemental Review Procedure)</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Doc no.</th>\n<th>Rev</th>\n<th>Date</th>\n<th>Owner</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>IS-BRAM-2025-06-25</td>\n<td>v1</td>\n<td>06/25/2025</td>\n<td>Interconnection 